{"raw": {"https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65377": {"title": "Adjunct Practicum Educator/Practicum Liaison, School of Social Work", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Adjunct Practicum Educator/Practicum Liaison, School of Social Work Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Adjunct Practicum Educator/Practicum Liaison, School of Social Work Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Adjunct Practicum Educator/Practicum Liaison, School of Social Work Department School of Social Work Posting Number F260062 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/63238 Employer State Faculty Appointment Term Temporary Position Type UUP Faculty Bargaining Unit Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2026-2027 Position Summary The School of Social Work at The University at Buffalo, State University of New York ( SUNY ) is seeking individuals with experience and knowledge of the social work practice community and the ability to make connections between the School\u2019s curriculum and the skills and practice knowledge gained in student practicums. The incumbent will work collaboratively with the Practicum Education Department to ensure quality practicum experiences that enable students to meet required competencies, and adhere to accreditation standards. Duties and Responsibilities (Practicum Educator): Provide a minimum of one hour per week of individual supervision to the MSW intern including an ongoing evaluation of their progress. Participate with the on-site task supervisor, in interviewing student interns for the practicum prior to the start of the actual practicum. Actively coordinate and work with on-site task supervisor in providing appropriate learning experiences for the interns. Attend an orientation session provided by the School (required for all new practicum educators). Provide the student with an orientation to the agency, including information on safety protocol, HIPAA requirements, or other regulations specific to practicum site. Duties and Responsibilities (Practicum Liaison): Reviewing and providing input to students and practicum educators regarding the learning contract. Making a minimum of one practicum visit during the fall semester and one during the spring semester for each of the assigned students. The visits should include a three-way meeting with the student and practicum educator at the practicum site. Be available to problem-solve issues with the student and/or practicum educator via phone or through additional practicum visits as needed; document any significant problems and the recommendations made to address the problem. Reviewing the Practicum Performance Evaluation Form completed by the practicum educator at mid-placement and at the end of the student\u2019s placement. This is a pooled posting, and positions are filled on an as-needed basis Outstanding Benefits Package Working at UB comes with benefits that exceed salary alone. There are personal rewards including comprehensive health and retirement plan options. We also focus on creating and sustaining a healthy mix of work, personal and academic pursuit \u2013 all in an effort to support your work-life effectiveness. We support your growth and development through our career coaching and training department and we qualify as a public service loan forgiveness organization. Learn more about our benefit packages . About The University at Buffalo The University at Buffalo (UB) #ubuffalo is one of America\u2019s leading public research universities and a flagship of the State University of New York system, recognized for our excellence and our impact. UB is a premier, research-intensive public university dedicated to academic excellence. Our research, creative activity and people positively impact the world. Like the city we call home, UB is distinguished by a culture of resilient optimism, resourceful thinking and pragmatic dreaming that enables us to reach others every day. Visit our website to learn more about the University at Buffalo . The University at Buffalo is an equal opportunity employer ( EOE ) and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with a disability. Minimum Qualifications Applicants must be licensed MSW\u2019s. Two or more years of relevant social work experience. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience supervising social work students preferred. Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Competitive Additional Salary Information Job Type Varies Campus North Campus Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Collen Long Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title Contact's Email cflong@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-645-1222 Posting Dates Posted 07/07/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled References Number of References Required 3 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a SUNY employee eligible for special consideration as a result of retrenchment? Yes No * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65343": {"title": "Academic Scholar - Clinical Assistant/ Associate Professor HS, Department of Medicine and Department of Pediatrics", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Academic Scholar - Clinical Assistant/ Associate Professor HS, Department of Medicine and Department of Pediatrics Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Academic Scholar - Clinical Assistant/ Associate Professor HS, Department of Medicine and Department of Pediatrics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Fiscal Year 2025-2026 Position Title Academic Scholar - Clinical Assistant/ Associate Professor HS, Department of Medicine and Department of Pediatrics Posting Category Faculty Department Medicine Posting Number U250082 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/59551 Employer University Affiliates Appointment Term Position Type Posting Detail Information Position Summary The University at Buffalo (UB), Jacobs School of Medicine and Biomedical Sciences, Department of Medicine and Department of Pediatrics, is seeking a board-certified or board-eligible Internal Medicine-Pediatrics (Med-Peds) Hospitalist for a full-time academic position. This unique dual role offers the opportunity to practice both adult and pediatric hospital medicine at Buffalo General Medical Center and John R. Oishei Children\u2019s Hospital, two premier institutions within the Kaleida Health system. Key Responsibilities Provide inpatient care to adult patients at Buffalo General Medical Center and pediatric patients at Oishei Children\u2019s Hospital Participate in teaching and supervision of medical students and residents from the Jacobs School of Medicine Collaborate with multidisciplinary teams in a dynamic, academic, and patient-centered environment Engage in scholarly activity, quality improvement, or clinical research as part of academic responsibilities Participate in departmental conferences, educational sessions, and faculty development opportunities Shared coverage of hospitalist services, including night and weekend responsibilities Why Join Us? Opportunity to practice in both adult and pediatric hospitalist setting Academic appointment through the Jacobs School of Medicine, with access to resources and support for scholarly work Collaborate with a vibrant, collegial group of physicians and educators Located in Buffalo, NY, a city experiencing a strong resurgence, with rich cultural life, affordable cost of living, and proximity to natural attractions like Niagara Falls and the Great Lakes About the University at Buffalo The University at Buffalo (UB) #ubuffalo is one of America\u2019s leading public research universities and a flagship of the State University of New York system, recognized for our excellence and our impact. UB is a premier, research-intensive public university dedicated to academic excellence. Our research, creative activity and people positively impact the world. Like the city we call home, UB is distinguished by a culture of resilient optimism, resourceful thinking and pragmatic dreaming that enables us to reach others every day. Visit our website to learn more about the University at Buffalo . The University at Buffalo is an equal opportunity employer ( EOE ) and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with a disability. Minimum Qualifications MD, DO, or equivalent degree Board certified or board eligible in Internal Medicine & Pediatrics Eligibility for unrestricted medical licensure in New York State. Commitment to academic medicine and teaching excellence Strong clinical and communication skills Interest in quality improvement and interdisciplinary collaboration Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Varies Additional Salary Information The salary range reflects our good faith and reasonable estimate of the possible compensation at the time of posting, the role and associated responsibilities, and the experience, education, and training of the selected candidate. Job Type Varies Campus As Assigned Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary REQUIRED : A cover letter outlining clinical and academic interests CV Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Ariel Burden Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title Staff Assistant Contact's Email aeburden@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-859-4848 Posting Dates Posted 10/15/2025 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled References Number of References Required 3 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65322": {"title": "Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor; Vascular Surgery", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor; Vascular Surgery Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor; Vascular Surgery Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor; Vascular Surgery Department Surgery Posting Number F260116 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65026 Employer State Faculty Appointment Term Term Position Type UUP Faculty Bargaining Unit 08 - UUP Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2026-2027 Position Summary The Department of Surgery within the Jacobs School of Medicine and Biomedical Sciences, State University of New York at Buffalo (UB), seeks qualified clinical educators, in Vascular Surgery, full-time positions based at major affiliated teaching hospitals. Appointment will be at the Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor , and rank will commensurate with experience. Overall duties include: serving as attending physician for inpatient services consultation and follow-up of patients teaching residents, fellows and medical students involvement in clinical and basic science research and participate in clinical trials About the University at Buffalo The University at Buffalo (UB) #ubuffalo is one of America\u2019s leading public research universities and a flagship of the State University of New York system, recognized for our excellence and our impact. UB is a premier, research-intensive public university dedicated to academic excellence. Our research, creative activity and people positively impact the world. Like the city we call home, UB is distinguished by a culture of resilient optimism, resourceful thinking and pragmatic dreaming that enables us to reach others every day. Visit our website to learn more about the University at Buffalo . The University at Buffalo is an equal opportunity employer ( EOE ) and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with a disability. Minimum Qualifications MD, DO, or equivalent degree Board Certified or Board Eligible in Vascular Surgery Fellowship training in Vascular Surgery Preferred Qualifications Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Competitive Additional Salary Information Job Type Varies Campus Buffalo General Hospital Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Nargis Hossain Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title Academic Programs Officer Contact's Email nhossain@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-859-7330 Posting Dates Posted 10/15/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled References Number of References Required 1 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs * Are you a SUNY employee eligible for special consideration as a result of retrenchment? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65306": {"title": "Academic Scholar - Clinical Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor; Department of OB-GYN", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Academic Scholar - Clinical Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor; Department of OB-GYN Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Academic Scholar - Clinical Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor; Department of OB-GYN Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Fiscal Year 2026-2027 Position Title Academic Scholar - Clinical Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor; Department of OB-GYN Posting Category Faculty Department Department of Obstetrics & Gynecology Posting Number U260091 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/64905 Employer University Affiliates Appointment Term Position Type Posting Detail Information Position Summary The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology (OB- GYN ) at the Jacobs School of Medicine and Biomedical Sciences is seeking a faculty member at the Clinical Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor level ( based on qualifications) that practices aspects of obstetrics and gynecology and can practice clinically and provide a combination of teaching students, residents and fellows, and participate in the administrative activities of the UB Department of OB- GYN . The precise balance of each of these activities is reviewed on an annual basis by the Department Chair and may shift according to the needs, interests and abilities of the candidate and the Department. About the University at Buffalo The University at Buffalo (UB) #ubuffalo is one of America\u2019s leading public research universities and a flagship of the State University of New York system, recognized for our excellence and our impact. UB is a premier, research-intensive public university dedicated to academic excellence. Our research, creative activity and people positively impact the world. Like the city we call home, UB is distinguished by a culture of resilient optimism, resourceful thinking and pragmatic dreaming that enables us to reach others every day. Visit our website to learn more about the University at Buffalo. The University at Buffalo is an equal opportunity employer ( EOE ) and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with a disability Minimum Qualifications MD, DO, or equivalent degree. NYS Medical License Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range $0.00 Additional Salary Information The salary range reflects our good faith and reasonable estimate of the possible compensation at the time of posting, the role and associated responsibilities, and the experience, education, and training of the selected candidate. Job Type Varies Campus Downtown Campus Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Molly Hartman Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title HR Operations Manager Contact's Email mahartma@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-829-5918 Posting Dates Posted 10/09/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled References Number of References Required 1 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65299": {"title": "Adult/Gerontology Nurse Practitioner Faculty", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Adult/Gerontology Nurse Practitioner Faculty Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Adult/Gerontology Nurse Practitioner Faculty Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Adult/Gerontology Nurse Practitioner Faculty Department School of Nursing Posting Number F260111 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/64585 Employer State Faculty Appointment Term Term Position Type UUP Faculty Bargaining Unit 08 - UUP Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2026-2027 Position Summary The University at Buffalo School of Nursing ( SON ) invites applicants to apply for a full-time (12 month) clinical position in the DNP Adult/Gerontology Nurse Practitioner ( AGNP ) program . Responsibilities include Classroom and online didactic teaching. Mentor, supervise, and evaluate students in clinical and simulated learning environments. Assist during admissions process with student application review and orientation. Collaborate with clinical placement coordinator to secure high-quality outpatient clinical sites for students. Perform clinical practicum site visits to evaluate student\u2019s clinical progress and facilitate and maintain relationships with preceptors. Facilitates and ensures safe, quality, interdisciplinary, evidence-based patient-centered care that is culturally sensitive, competent, ethical, and compassionate throughout students practical, classroom, online, simulated learning experiences and IPE courses. Maintain an active record of extracurricular activities and encourage student participation with faculty when possible. Contribute to new nursing knowledge through scholarship activities and student mentoring. Provides service through participation in School of Nursing and University wide committees, and faculty governance as well as active membership in professional local, national, and international organizations. Maintain clinical nursing expertise and certification. We are particularly looking for candidates who can operate effectively in a diverse community of students and faculty and share our vision of helping all constituents reach their full potential. We are committed to developing an excellent and diverse community of scholars and students engaged in education, research, and service. We encourage applications from women, members of historically marginalized groups, veterans, and individuals with disabilities. About UB School of Nursing Founded in 1936, UB School of Nursing is a leader in high-quality nursing education and research in a dynamic university setting. Our mission continues our scholarly excellence as we educate clinical leaders, conduct impactful research, and deliver clinical care based upon principles of collaboration, equity, inclusion, and social justice for our region and the world. Our undergraduate programs prepare nurses for expanded professional roles in an increasingly complex and evolving health care environment, and our graduate and advanced certificate programs prepare clinicians, researchers, educators and leaders to provide complex care across settings, educate the next generation of nurses, and advance nursing and health care knowledge. Learn more: Our benefits , where we prioritize your well-being and success to enhance every aspect of your life. Being a part of the University at Buffalo community. The University at Buffalo is an equal opportunity employer ( EOE ) and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with a disability. Minimum Qualifications PhD or DNP degree from a regionally accredited School of Nursing. Current national certification as an AGNP or ANP . Current New York State RN license. Minimum 3 years\u2019 experience practicing as an AGNP / ANP . Excellent clinical and interpersonal skills with ability to work as a multidisciplinary healthcare team member. Maintain clinical practice in specialty areas. Preferred Qualifications Previous experience teaching at the DNP level. Clinical simulation/practicum student supervision. AGNP -PC or dual-certified AGNP -AC. Established record of research and scholarship activity. Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Competitive Additional Salary Information Job Type Full-Time Campus South Campus Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Jackie Martek Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title Senior Staff Assistant Contact's Email jmartek@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-829-3537 Posting Dates Posted 10/02/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled References Number of References Required 3 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs * Are you a SUNY employee eligible for special consideration as a result of retrenchment? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65297": {"title": "Clinical Assistant Professor, Periodontics and Endodontics", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Clinical Assistant Professor, Periodontics and Endodontics Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Clinical Assistant Professor, Periodontics and Endodontics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Clinical Assistant Professor, Periodontics and Endodontics Department Department of Periodontics and Endodontics Posting Number F260107 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/64457 Employer State Faculty Appointment Term Term Position Type UUP Faculty Bargaining Unit 08 - UUP Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2026-2027 Position Summary The School of Dental Medicine Periodontics and Endodontics department is seeking full time faculty members to provide instruction in the preclinical and clinical courses, DDS or Advanced Education Students in the area of Periodontics . In this position, you will: Provide proficient instruction in all periodontics discipline Provide lectures in didactic courses Provide clinical demonstrations Learn more: Our benefits , where we prioritize your well-being and success to enhance every aspect of your life. Being a part of the University at Buffalo community. The University at Buffalo is an equal opportunity employer ( EOE ) and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with a disability. Minimum Qualifications DDS or DMD equivalent Post-graduate certificate in Periodontology Preferred Qualifications New York State licensure or eligibility At least 1 year of academic/teaching experience in the USA or Canada in the last 5 years Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Commensurate with Experience Additional Salary Information Job Type Full-Time Campus South Campus Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? Yes Background Check Notification For non-internal applicants: a selected candidate will have to complete and pass a background check prior to appointment. Contact Information Contact's Name Victoria Balazs Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title Program Coordinator Contact's Email vmbalazs@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-829-6643 Posting Dates Posted 09/28/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled References Number of References Required 3 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs * Are you a SUNY employee eligible for special consideration as a result of retrenchment? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65295": {"title": "Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor; Department of OB-GYN", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor; Department of OB-GYN Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor; Department of OB-GYN Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor; Department of OB-GYN Department Department of Obstetrics & Gynecology Posting Number F260101 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/64242 Employer State Faculty Appointment Term Term Position Type UUP Faculty Bargaining Unit 08 - UUP Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2026-2027 Position Summary The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology is seeking a physician with subspecialty training in Urogynecology and Reconstructive Pelvic Surgery ( URPS ) to join our team at the Jacobs School of Medicine and Biomedical Sciences, University at Buffalo (UB), SUNY . Our partners include Kaleida Health and Erie County Medical Center. UB is a top-tier academic institution, situated across 3 campuses, with faculty engaged in transformational patient care, education, and medical research. The successful applicant will be BC/BE in Obstetrics and Gynecology and have completed a formal fellowship in Urogynecology and Reconstructive Pelvic Surgery ( URPS ) . In this position you will be expected to: possess excellent clinical skills, provide the highest quality of patient care demonstrate capability, interest, and enthusiasm for teaching medical students and training residents. Our residency has 36 categorical positions, 9 at each year, and Jacobs School of Medicine and Biomedical Sciences has about 200 medical students per year. Our goal is to augment our current Division of URPS . Involvement in clinical research is encouraged, and there are many opportunities for interdisciplinary research within the Buffalo Niagara Medical Campus and the larger University at Buffalo community. Academic rank and compensation will be commensurate with training and achievement. A comprehensive benefit package is included. Buffalo, New York, is known as \u201cThe City of Good Neighbors\u201d and is the second largest city in New York State. It has many unique characteristics, which make it an ideal place to live and work. Amherst, a nearby suburb, is consistently rated as one of the safest communities in the nation. Area public schools are outstanding, and housing is very affordable. Buffalo is a cultural center with excellent theater, engaging museums, and an exceptional symphony. In addition, the surrounding environment contains two of the Great Lakes for sailing, boating and fishing; hills for skiing and hiking; award-winning local restaurants for dining out; and the breathtaking Niagara Falls for admiring and exploring. Learn more: Our benefits , where we prioritize your well-being and success to enhance every aspect of your life. Being a part of the University at Buffalo community. The University at Buffalo is an equal opportunity employer ( EOE ) and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with a disability. Minimum Qualifications MD, DO, or equivalent degree Preferred Qualifications BC/BE in Obstetrics and Gynecology and subspecialty BC/BE in Urogynecology and Reconstructive Pelvic Surgery ( URPS ) Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Competitive Additional Salary Information Job Type Varies Campus Downtown Campus Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Brendan Tom Contact's Pronouns He/him/his Contact's Title Director of Human Resources, Jacobs School of Medicine and Biomedical Sciences Contact's Email bjtom@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-829-2771 Posting Dates Posted 09/09/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled References Number of References Required 3 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs * Are you a SUNY employee eligible for special consideration as a result of retrenchment? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65294": {"title": "Clinical Assistant Professor (10 Month), Nutrition", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Clinical Assistant Professor (10 Month), Nutrition Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Clinical Assistant Professor (10 Month), Nutrition Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Clinical Assistant Professor (10 Month), Nutrition Department Department of Exercise and Nutrition Sciences Posting Number F260095 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/64103 Employer State Faculty Appointment Term Term Position Type UUP Faculty Bargaining Unit 08 - UUP Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2026-2027 Position Summary The Department of Exercise and Nutrition Sciences within the School of Public Health and Health Professions invites applicants for a full-time, 10-month Clinical Assistant Professor position in our Nutrition Program . This is a clinical faculty position to begin in August 2027. Key Responsibilities: Primarily teach in the undergraduate Nutrition Program, but may have opportunities to teach in other programs for the Department. Empower the next generation of nutrition professionals by offering personalized academic advising, career mentorship, and meaningful guidance to both students and teaching assistants. Shape the future of the curriculum through innovative course design, continuous program enhancement, and thoughtful evaluation that keeps our offerings cutting edge and relevant. Play an active role in advancing the department and the profession by contributing your talents to committees, initiatives, and service activities across the Department, School, University, and professional organizations. Foster a collaborative, supportive academic community by modeling collegiality, teamwork, and a spirit of shared purpose in all faculty interactions. Engage deeply in teaching excellence, with a commitment to delivering up to 12 credit hours each Fall and Spring semester in a dynamic, student centered environment. About the Department: The Department of Exercise and Nutrition Sciences is a dynamic, research driven academic unit within the School of Public Health and Health Professions . Faculty and students collaborate across well established research programs supported by excellent facilities and a wide range of academic offerings\u2014from undergraduate degrees in Exercise and Nutritional Sciences to advanced MS and PhD programs. The Department offers a BS in Exercise Science, a BS in Nutritional Sciences, a BS/MS in Exercise Nutrition, an MS in Clinical Nutrition leading to the Registered Dietitian credential, an MS degree in Athletic Training, MS degrees in Nutrition and Exercise Science and PhD degrees in Exercise Science and Nutrition. A signature feature of the department is the Center for Research and Education in Special Environments ( CRESE ) , a state of the art facility that enables cutting edge research at altitude, underwater, and in extreme temperatures. It\u2019s an exciting environment for faculty who want to innovate, mentor, and make a meaningful impact in the fields of nutrition and human performance. Learn more: Our benefits , where we prioritize your well-being and success to enhance every aspect of your life. Being a part of the University at Buffalo community. The University at Buffalo is an equal opportunity employer ( EOE ) and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with a disability. Minimum Qualifications Earned PhD in Nutrition or related field; OR Doctor of Clinical Nutrition ( DCN ) with 2 years teaching experience Evidence of teaching experience in nutrition or closely related areas such as biochemistry, pathophysiology of chronic diseases, epidemiology, or health behavior Preferred Qualifications Postdoctoral research training Record of peer-reviewed scientific publications consistent with experience Credentialed as a registered dietitian nutritionist ( RDN ) by the Commission on Dietetic Registration Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range $70,000 - $80,000 Additional Salary Information Job Type Full-Time Campus South Campus Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Benjamin Stich Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title Department Resource Manager Contact's Email bstich@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-829-2048 Posting Dates Posted 08/31/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled 09/01/2027 References Number of References Required 3 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs * Are you a SUNY employee eligible for special consideration as a result of retrenchment? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65293": {"title": "Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor, Neuromuscular Disorders; Department of Neurology", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor, Neuromuscular Disorders; Department of Neurology Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor, Neuromuscular Disorders; Department of Neurology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor, Neuromuscular Disorders; Department of Neurology Department Neurology Posting Number F260081 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/63697 Employer State Faculty Appointment Term Term Position Type UUP Faculty Bargaining Unit 08 - UUP Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2026-2027 Position Summary The University at Buffalo, State University of New York, Department of Neurology is expanding and adding to its clinical faculty. Wea are actively recruiting for a BC/BE neurologist, fellowship trained in neuromuscular disorders . Rank at Clinical Assistant or Clinical Associate level will commensurate with experience This candidate will provide inpatient care for general neurology patients at Buffalo General Medical Center. Candidates will be responsible for call every other day while on hospital service. They will have an outpatient neuromuscular disorders clinic at either our Williamsville or Conventus locations. Faculty duties include education, oversight and instruction of neurology residents, fellows, and medical students from Jacobs School of Medicine and Biomedical Sciences. Learn more: Our benefits , where we prioritize your well-being and success to enhance every aspect of your life. Being a part of the University at Buffalo community. The University at Buffalo is an equal opportunity employer ( EOE ) and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with a disability. Minimum Qualifications M.D., D.O., or equivalent degree BC/BE in Neurology Fellowship trained in Neuromuscular Disorders Preferred Qualifications Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Competitive Additional Salary Information Job Type Part-Time Campus Downtown Campus Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary Please include a brief cover letter explaining your interest in the position. Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Thomas Bellanca Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title Assistant to the Chair Contact's Email tjbellan@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-323-0646 Posting Dates Posted 08/03/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled References Number of References Required 3 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment oppo