g Unit 08 - UUP Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2026-2027 Position Summary The School of Social Work at the University at Buffalo is searching for a faculty colleague to join our school in a tenure-track faculty position as an Assistant or Associate Professor . The successful candidate for this position will have: A doctorate in Social Work or a related discipline An MSW with practice experience An active research agenda Experience having taught social work courses in seated, online, and hybrid environments. Duties include: Conducting fundable research. Teaching in the school\u2019s degree programs. Engaging in cross-disciplinary collaboration with university colleagues. Participating on school committees. Applicants are expected to have a scholarly record appropriate for the rank to which they are applying. To learn why the UB School of Social Work may be the right career choice for you, visit our website . Learn more: Our benefits , where we prioritize your well-being and success to enhance every aspect of your life. Being a part of the University at Buffalo community. The University at Buffalo is an equal opportunity employer ( EOE ) and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with a disability. Minimum Qualifications PhD in social work or a related field MSW or a masters degree in a related field Preferred Qualifications PhD in social work or social welfare MSW and two years of post- MSW practice experience Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Competitive Additional Salary Information Job Type Full-Time Campus North Campus Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Robert Keefe Contact's Pronouns He/him/his Contact's Title Associate Professor Contact's Email rhkeefe@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 58