 faculty. The Department of Mathematics is on UB\u2019s North Campus in suburban Amherst, an area that combines outstanding public schools and services with a low cost of living. Downtown Buffalo, with its eclectic neighborhoods, the Lake Erie waterfront, and vast cultural resources, is 15 minutes away, and Niagara Falls is also just 20 minutes away. The University at Buffalo (UB) is one of America\u2019s leading public research universities and a flagship of the State University of New York system, recognized for our excellence and our impact. UB is a premier, research-intensive public university dedicated to academic excellence. Our research, creative activity and people positively impact the world. Like the city we call home, UB is distinguished by a culture of resilient optimism, resourceful thinking, and pragmatic dreaming that enables us to reach others every day. Visit our website to learn more about the University at Buffalo. Learn more: Our benefits , where we prioritize your well-being and success to enhance every aspect of your life. Being a part of the University at Buffalo community. The University at Buffalo is an equal opportunity employer ( EOE ) and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with a disability. Minimum Qualifications PhD in mathematics or a related field; Excellent research accomplishments; A strong commitment to teaching. Preferred Qualifications Postdoctoral experience is preferred. Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Competitive Additional Salary Information Job Type Full-Time Campus North Campus Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary Candidates must submit a cover letter and curriculum vitae at https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/64020 Candidates should also submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, a summary of their research program, a description of their teaching experience, and at least four reference letters, one of which supports the applicant\u2019s effectiveness as a teacher, to https://www.mathjobs.org/jobs/list/28763 . The deadline for applications is October 16, 2026. Late applications will be considered until the position is filled. Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Barbara Prinari Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title Professor Contact's Email bprinari@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-645-8799 Posting Dates Posted 08/24/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled 08/16/2027 References Number of References Required 1 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs * Are you a SUNY employee eligible for special consideration as a result of retrenchment? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65200": {"title": "Open Rank Tenure/Tenure-Track Faculty, Strategy", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Open Rank Tenure/Tenure-Track Faculty, Strategy Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Open Rank Tenure/Tenure-Track Faculty, Strategy Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Open Rank Tenure/Tenure-Track Faculty, Strategy Department Operations Management and Strategy Posting Number F260097 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/64201 Employer State Faculty Appointment Term Term Position Type UUP Faculty Bargaining Unit 08 - UUP Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2026-2027 Position Summary The University at Buffalo (UB), a flagship institution of the State University of New York and a member of the Association of American Universities ( AAU ), invites applications for a tenure-track/tenured position in Strategy at the Assistant or Associate Professor level in the Department of Operations Management and Strategy within the School of Management, with a preference for candidates at the Associate Professor level. We seek an accomplished scholar whose research advances knowledge in strategic management and contributes to the School of Management\u2019s mission of producing impactful research, delivering innovative business education, and engaging with organizations and communities locally and globally. For full consideration, required application materials should be formally submitted by December 15th, 2026. Faculty obligation will begin mid-August 2027. The successful candidate will be expected to: Have an outstanding record of influential scholarship, as evidenced by a strong publication and citation record. Publish in leading scholarly journals and contribute to the advancement of knowledge in areas such as competitive strategy, corporate strategy, entrepreneurship, innovation, international business, sustainability, technology strategy, or related fields. Teach doctoral, MBA , master\u2019s, and undergraduate courses in strategy and related disciplines. Specific courses may include Managerial Economics and Macro Economics, Strategy, and/or Entrepreneurship. Contribute to executive and professional education initiatives. Mentor doctoral students and junior faculty members. Provide academic leadership within the department, school, and university. Contribute to curriculum development and strategic initiatives within the School of Management. Build collaborations across UB and with external stakeholders, including industry, government, and academic partners. Participate actively in professional organizations and the broader scholarly community. About the Department The Department of Operations Management and Strategy is home to distinguished faculty conducting impactful research in strategic management, entrepreneurship, international business, operations management, and supply chain management. The department supports doctoral specialization in strategic management and provides a collaborative intellectual environment that encourages innovative and interdisciplinary scholarship. About the School of Management The University at Buffalo School of Management is one of the nation\u2019s leading public business schools. The school is committed to transformative education, thought leadership, and meaningful engagement with business and society. Faculty members engage in research that addresses important managerial and societal challenges while preparing future leaders through exceptional educational experiences. Learn more: Our benefits , where we prioritize your well-being and success to enhance every aspect of your life. Being a part of the University at Buffalo community. The University at Buffalo is an equal opportunity employer ( EOE ) and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with a disability. Minimum Qualifications Assistant Professor Doctoral degree (PhD) in a business discipline or related field. A research portfolio if applying for an Assistant Professor position A record of influential scholarship at a major research university if applying for an Associate position, including a strong publication record in top journals in Strategy. Associate Professor Doctoral degree (PhD) in a business discipline or related field. Demonstrated record of high-quality scholarly research with publications in peer-reviewed journals recognized within the field. Evidence of effective teaching at the undergraduate and/or graduate level. Qualifications consistent with appointment at the rank of Associate Professor with tenure at a major research university. Preferred Qualifications Research that addresses contemporary strategic challenges facing organizations and society. Ability to engage in interdisciplinary collaborations across business and related fields. Experience securing externally funded research or leading major research initiatives. An interest in developing the research and outreach capability of research and practice centers. Evidence of commitment to fostering an inclusive and collaborative academic environment. Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Competitive Additional Salary Information Job Type Full-Time Campus As Assigned Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Erika Bagnoli Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title Contact's Email erikabag@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-645-3221 Posting Dates Posted 09/08/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled 09/01/2027 References Number of References Required 3 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs * Are you a SUNY employee eligible for special consideration as a result of retrenchment? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Summary of Courses Taught Teaching Evaluations Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research Philosophy Optional Documents Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65199": {"title": "Assistant Professor in Pediatric Speech Production", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Assistant Professor in Pediatric Speech Production Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Assistant Professor in Pediatric Speech Production Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Professor in Pediatric Speech Production Department Department of Communicative Disorders and Sciences Posting Number F260099 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/64267 Employer State Faculty Appointment Term Position Type UUP Faculty Bargaining Unit 08 - UUP Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2026-2027 Position Summary The Department of Communicative Disorders and Sciences ( CDS ) at the University at Buffalo, The State University of New York (UB) invites applications for a full-time, 10-month, academic faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor . We seek a scholar with expertise in pediatric speech production, including speech sound disorders, childhood dysarthria, and childhood apraxia of speech. The appointment will begin in Fall 2027. The primary responsibilities of this position include (1) developing a program of extramurally funded research; (2) teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels; and (3) serving the Department, College, University, profession, and community. The Department of Communicative Disorders and Sciences at the University at Buffalo is committed to excellence in research, teaching, and service and to fostering an inclusive academic environment. UB is a member of the Association of American Universities ( AAU ). With support from the College of Arts and Sciences, the department is committed to building existing research, clinical, and academic capacities to continue to provide leadership in the fields of speech-language pathology, hearing science, and related disorders. The UB Audiology and Speech Pathology clinic is located next to the department, and collaborations between clinical and academic faculty are encouraged. The university provides strong support for research productivity including pre- and post-award administration, purchasing, and hiring. The Western New York region is a large and diverse area, and the CDS department has strong connections with local schools, speech-language pathologists, and organizations serving children. For additional information about the Department of Communicative Disorders and Sciences, please visit the University at Buffalo Department of Communicative Disorders and Sciences website. Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in speech sciences, communication sciences and disorders, or a closely related field by the time of appointment. Research expertise in pediatric speech production. Preferred Qualifications: Certification of the American Speech-Language-Hearing Association or other clinical training Teaching experience at the college-level Qualified applicants must submit: A cover letter Curriculum vitae Research statement Teaching statement Three letters of recommendation Applications must be submitted through UB Jobs https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/64267 . Applications received by October 15, 2026 will receive priority consideration. Questions about the position may be directed to the Search Committee Chair Dr. Ling-Yu Guo ( lingyugu@buffalo.edu ). Learn more: Our benefits , where we prioritize your well-being and success to enhance every aspect of your life. Being a part of the University at Buffalo community. The University at Buffalo is an equal opportunity employer ( EOE ) and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with a disability. Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. in speech sciences, communication sciences and disorders, or a closely related field conferred by the time of appointment. Research expertise in pediatric speech production. Preferred Qualifications Certification of the American Speech-Language-Hearing Association or other clinical training Teaching experience at the college-level Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Competitive Additional Salary Information Job Type Full-Time Campus South Campus Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary All application materials should be submitted via UB Jobs. Application materials submitted directly to the posting contact will not be acknowledged and cannot be considered. Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Ling-Yu Guo Contact's Pronouns He/Him Contact's Title Associate Professor Contact's Email lingyugu@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-829-5567 Posting Dates Posted 09/10/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled 08/16/2027 References Number of References Required 3 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant By providing the names and e-mail addresses of my references, I hereby authorize either Human Resources or the applicable hiring department to contact my references via e-mail to request a reference letter on my behalf. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs * Are you a SUNY employee eligible for special consideration as a result of retrenchment? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Research Statement Teaching Statement Optional Documents Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65198": {"title": "Academic Scholar- Clinical Assistant/ Associate Professor, Division of Geriatrics &amp; Palliative Medicine", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Academic Scholar- Clinical Assistant/ Associate Professor, Division of Geriatrics &amp; Palliative Medicine Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Academic Scholar- Clinical Assistant/ Associate Professor, Division of Geriatrics & Palliative Medicine Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Fiscal Year 2025-2026 Position Title Academic Scholar- Clinical Assistant/ Associate Professor, Division of Geriatrics & Palliative Medicine Posting Category Faculty Department Medicine Posting Number U250010 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/55559 Employer University Affiliates Appointment Term Position Type Posting Detail Information Position Summary Division of Geriatrics & Palliative Medicine , Jacobs School of Medicine ( JSMBS ) and Biomedical Sciences, University at Buffalo (UB), seeks a Geriatric BE/BC physician for a full-time position based at our suburban practice. The qualified candidate will be appointed at the Clinical Assistant/ Associate Professor level. The candidate will be responsible for the development and oversight of an ambulatory practice that provides comprehensive evaluation and care to a geriatric population. The candidate will provide direct care as well as supervise other members of the care team. This is a unique opportunity to build a state-of-the-art experience for the elderly in a community based multispecialty setting. Given the academic mission of the Division the candidate will oversee the educational experience of fellows, residents and medical students assigned to the site. This is an opportunity to join an organization focused on the future of medicine-one whose physicians and advanced practitioners collaborate with their patients to ensure a higher state of care and better outcomes. At UB Department of Medicine, you will experience a deeper sense of compassion, greater breadth of diversity and a never-ending desire to raise the standard of medical excellence, regionally and nationally. We are committed to a professional environment that is positive, respectful, cohesive and supportive of cultural and individual differences in the service of our clinical and academic goals. About The University at Buffalo The University at Buffalo (UB) #ubuffalo is one of America\u2019s leading public research universities and a flagship of the State University of New York system, recognized for our excellence and our impact. UB is a premier, research-intensive public university dedicated to academic excellence. Our research, creative activity and people positively impact the world. Like the city we call home, UB is distinguished by a culture of resilient optimism, resourceful thinking and pragmatic dreaming that enables us to reach others every day. Visit our website to learn more about the University at Buffalo. University at Buffalo and UBMD IM \u201cDBA as AMS\u201d is an equal opportunity employer ( EOE ) and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with a disability. Minimum Qualifications MD/DO BE/BC in Geriatric Medicine Preferred Qualifications BE/BC in Palliative Medicine Eligible for medical licensure in the State of New York Current and unrestricted DEA Certificate Currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range $0.00 Additional Salary Information The salary range reflects our good faith and reasonable estimate of the possible compensation at the time of posting, the role and associated responsibilities, and the experience, education, and training of the selected candidate. Job Type Full-Time Campus Off site location Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary All applicants must apply via UB Jobs. For your references, please provide a minimum of 2 professional contacts. Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Dory Prouty Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title Senior Human Resources Generalist Contact's Email dc62@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-961-9914 Posting Dates Posted 01/30/2025 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled References Number of References Required 3 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65197": {"title": "Assistant Teaching Professor, Economics (Non-Tenure-Track)", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Assistant Teaching Professor, Economics (Non-Tenure-Track) Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Assistant Teaching Professor, Economics (Non-Tenure-Track) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Teaching Professor, Economics (Non-Tenure-Track) Department Department of Economics Posting Number F260100 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/64268 Employer State Faculty Appointment Term Position Type UUP Faculty Bargaining Unit 08 - UUP Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2026-2027 Position Summary The Department of Economics at the University at Buffalo, The State University of New York, seeks to fill one Assistant Teaching Professor (Non-Tenure-Track) position for an economist committed to achieving excellence in instruction. The position requires teaching 3 undergraduate courses each semester, including large-enrollment introductory courses, and some departmental service. We are seeking candidates committed to developing careers in economics education. This is a full-time, non-tenure-track qualified rank faculty position (10-month obligation) ideally beginning with UB\u2019s spring 2027 semester, though fall 2027 start is possible. The initial appointment will be for 3 years, with renewable 1-year terms. JEL Classifications: \u2022 00 \u2013 Default: Any field \u2022 A1 \u2013 General Economics \u2022 A2 \u2013 Economic Education and Teaching of Economics Applications received by October 11, 2026 will receive priority consideration. The position will remain open until filled. If you have questions, please email the posting contact, and indicate \u201cAssistant Teaching Professor Position\u201d in the subject of the email. Applications must be submitted through UB Jobs https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/64268 . Learn more: Our benefits , where we prioritize your well-being and success to enhance every aspect of your life. Being a part of the University at Buffalo community. The University at Buffalo is an equal opportunity employer ( EOE ) and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with a disability. Minimum Qualifications PhD in Economics in hand at the time of initial appointment Teaching experience in a higher education setting Preferred Qualifications Experience leading experiential learning programs in higher education settings Experience teaching introductory and large-enrollment courses Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Competitive Additional Salary Information Job Type Full-Time Campus North Campus Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary Applications received by October 11, 2026 will receive priority consideration. If including an optional Writing Sample please provide a research paper or other evidence of effective written communication. If you have questions, please email the posting contact, and indicate \u201cAssistant Teaching Professor Position\u201d in the subject of the email. All application materials must be submitted via UB Jobs. Application materials submitted directly to the posting contact will not be acknowledged and cannot be considered. Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Todd Pugatch Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title Associate Professor Contact's Email ecomain@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-645-8670 Posting Dates Posted 09/10/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled 01/07/2027 References Number of References Required 3 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant By providing the names and e-mail addresses of my references, I hereby authorize either Human Resources or the applicable hiring department to contact my references via e-mail to request a reference letter on my behalf. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs * Are you a SUNY employee eligible for special consideration as a result of retrenchment? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Documentation of Teaching Effectiveness Sample Syllabus Optional Documents Writing Sample Additional Supporting Documentation Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65196": {"title": "Teaching Faculty (Non-Tenure Track), Marketing and Behavioral Research Lab", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Teaching Faculty (Non-Tenure Track), Marketing and Behavioral Research Lab Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Teaching Faculty (Non-Tenure Track), Marketing and Behavioral Research Lab Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Teaching Faculty (Non-Tenure Track), Marketing and Behavioral Research Lab Department Department of Marketing Posting Number F260103 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/64318 Employer State Faculty Appointment Term Position Type UUP Faculty Bargaining Unit 08 - UUP Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2026-2027 Position Summary The Department of Marketing in the School of Management at the University at Buffalo (UB), a flagship member of the State University of New York ( SUNY ) system and a leading public research university, invites applications for a non-tenure-track qualified faculty position in Marketing Department. This position offers an exciting opportunity to contribute to the School of Management through excellence in teaching, service, and, for qualified candidates, leadership of the School\u2019s Behavioral Research Lab. Primary teaching responsibilities will include the delivery of eight to nine courses annually in marketing or related areas. Service expectations include active engagement with the department, school, university, and broader community through activities such as advising student organizations, serving on committees, and supporting outreach initiatives. In addition to teaching responsibilities, the department welcomes applications from candidates interested and qualified to serve as Manager of the Behavioral Research Lab. In this leadership role, the successful candidate will provide strategic direction and operational oversight for behavioral research activities that support faculty, doctoral students, and other researchers across the School of Management. The ideal candidate will possess expertise at the intersection of behavioral science and industry engagement, serving as a key liaison among faculty researchers, corporate partners, and advanced biometric and behavioral research technologies. The department seeks to fill this position immediately and will consider candidates for either a teaching-focused faculty appointment or a combined teaching and lab management role. Depending on the responsibilities assigned, the appointment may be structured as either an academic year or a 12-month position. For full consideration, applicants should submit their application materials by October 16, 2026. Review of applications will begin immediately, and the position will remain open until filled. Primary Responsibilities Teaching Teach undergraduate and graduate marketing courses Maintain excellence in classroom instruction and student engagement. Participate in curriculum development and continuous improvement initiatives. Mentor students and support experiential learning opportunities. Service Participate in departmental, school, and university service activities. Support outreach efforts and partnerships with industry and community organizations. Contribute to initiatives that enhance the national visibility of the Department of Marketing and the School of Management. Responsibilities Specific to the Behavioral Research Lab Corporate Consulting & Project Management Design and execute research strategies to address complex business questions utilizing various methodologies. Author Statements of Work (SOWs), define project timelines, establish budgets, and manage client deliverables. Prepare highly visual, executive-ready presentations featuring actionable design directives. Lab Management Manage the day-to-day operations of the Behavioral Research Lab. Recruit, train, and supervise graduate and undergraduate research assistants. Develop and maintain participant recruitment systems and research databases. Ensure compliance with institutional policies, human-subjects research requirements, and ethical research standards. Maintain laboratory equipment, iMotions software, and research resources. Research Design and Execution Support Collaborate with faculty and graduate students on behavioral and consumer research projects. Provide expertise in study design, survey development, experimental methodology, and data collection procedures. Support grant-funded and externally sponsored research initiatives. Facilitate implementation of behavioral, consumer, and decision-making studies. Analysis and Reporting Conduct or support quantitative and qualitative data analysis. Develop reports that deliver results and insights. Assist researchers in interpreting findings and communicating results to academic and industry audiences. Maintain documentation and reporting systems related to laboratory activities and outcomes. Learn more: Our benefits , where we prioritize your well-being and success to enhance every aspect of your life. Being a part of the University at Buffalo community. The University at Buffalo is an equal opportunity employer ( EOE ) and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with a disability. Minimum Qualifications Master\u2019s degree or Ph.D. in Human-Computer Interaction ( HCI ), UX Research, Cognitive Psychology, Marketing Analytics, or a related marketing or behavioral science field. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated experience designing and conducting behavioral or consumer research studies. Proven track record of managing paid corporate consulting projects, user testing, or market research studies. Technical Expertise: 1- 3 years of hands-on experience utilizing iMotions software and integrating eye-tracking hardware (e.g., Tobii, Pupil Labs). Familiarity with supplementary UX tools (e.g., Figma, Adobe XD, Hotjar) and advanced statistical software ( SPSS , R, Python). Experience with advanced biosensors such as EEG or facial expression coding (Affectiva/ FACET ). Prior teaching experience at the university-level. PhD in Marketing, Consumer Behavior, Psychology, Behavioral Science, or a related field. Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Competitive Additional Salary Information Job Type Full-Time Campus North Campus Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary As part of the Research Statement, please include a statement describing experience with behavioral research and laboratory management. Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Erika Bagnoli Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title Contact's Email erikabag@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-645-3221 Posting Dates Posted 09/14/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled 01/04/2027 References Number of References Required 3 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs * Are you a SUNY employee eligible for special consideration as a result of retrenchment? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Research Statement Optional Documents Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65195": {"title": "Academic Scholar - Clinical Assistant Professor, Department of Pathology and Anatomical Sciences", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Academic Scholar - Clinical Assistant Professor, Department of Pathology and Anatomical Sciences Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Academic Scholar - Clinical Assistant Professor, Department of Pathology and Anatomical Sciences Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Fiscal Year 2024-2025 Position Title Academic Scholar - Clinical Assistant Professor, Department of Pathology and Anatomical Sciences Posting Category Faculty Department Department of Pathology and Anatomical Sciences Posting Number U240082 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/53695 Employer University Affiliates Appointment Term Position Type Posting Detail Information Position Summary The Department of Pathology and Anatomical Sciences in Jacobs School of Medicine and Biomedical Sciences is seeking applicants for Academic Scholars . Candidates will be required to perform all the duties of an attending pathologists which include: General and subspecialty pathology Autopsy pathology Select areas of laboratory medicine Frozen sections Areas of expertise in oncological pathology, GI, GU, GYN , or Derm are desirable Pathologists additionally attend and actively participate in: Tumor board Residency teaching and oversight Medical/Dental undergraduate educational teaching About The University at Buffalo The University at Buffalo (UB) #ubuffalo is one of America\u2019s leading public research universities and a flagship of the State University of New York system, recognized for our excellence and our impact. UB is a premier, research-intensive public university dedicated to academic excellence. Our research, creative activity and people positively impact the world. Like the city we call home, UB is distinguished by a culture of resilient optimism, resourceful thinking and pragmatic dreaming that enables us to reach others every day. Visit our website to learn more about the University at Buffalo . The University at Buffalo is an equal opportunity employer ( EOE ) and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with a disability. Minimum Qualifications MD, DO, or equivalent Board Certified or Board Eligible Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range $0.00 Additional Salary Information The salary range reflects our good faith and reasonable estimate of the possible compensation at the time of posting, the role and associated responsibilities, and the experience, education, and training of the selected candidate. Job Type Full-Time Campus University Affiliated Hospitals Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Anna Elkin Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title Chief Operating Officer Contact's Email aelkin@kaleidahealth.org Contact's Phone 716-626-7944 Posting Dates Posted 10/28/2024 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled References Number of References Required 1 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter CV/Resume Optional Documents Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65170": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor, School of Social Work", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Adjunct Instructor, School of Social Work Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Adjunct Instructor, School of Social Work Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Adjunct Instructor, School of Social Work Department School of Social Work Posting Number F260063 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/63237 Employer State Faculty Appointment Term Temporary Position Type UUP Faculty Bargaining Unit Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2026-2027 Position Summary The University at Buffalo School of Social Work is looking for exceptional part-time Adjunct Instructors who are dedicated to providing quality educational experiences to our Doctor of Social Work ( DSW ), Master of Social Work ( MSW ) and Undergraduate students. The successful candidate will deliver courses by utilizing the Brightspace platform, also known as UBLearns. DSW : The DSW program is delivered fully online. The successful candidate will deliver courses using advanced technologies. For a description of the DSW program and a list of course offerings, please visit the DSW program website . MSW & Undergraduate: For a list of course offerings, please visit the MSW program website and Undergraduate education website . The MSW Program is specifically interested in candidates with a strong teaching record and experience teaching online. Please view the special instructions summary for the contact information for each of the programs. We are looking for adjunct faculty to help implement our curriculum and teach essential social work history, theory, competencies, and skill. Responsibilities include: Teaching course content and using the course description and objectives (from a master course syllabus). Instructors will need to develop a full syllabus, following the Syllabi Requirements outlined in the School\u2019s Handbook. Instructors are also required to utilize the learning management system, Brightspace. Instructors should be familiar with the School\u2019s TI-HR curriculum to help facilitate and advance students\u2019 skills, competency, and knowledge development. Attend (in-person or virtually) meetings in the fall and spring semesters. Function and communicate effectively and respectfully within the context of varying beliefs, behaviors, orientations, identities, and cultural backgrounds. Maintain a strong commitment to Social Work\u2019s ethics and values, as well as the School\u2019s mission, values, and vision. Collaborate with students and school administration effectively to support students. This is a pooled posting, and positions are filled on an as-needed basis. The University at Buffalo is an equal opportunity employer ( EOE ) and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with a disability. Minimum Qualifications Two or more years of relevant social work experience post- MSW degree. Knowledge of the American Psychological Association ( APA ) reference citation style. For the DSW program: Doctorate degree. For the MSW & Undergraduate program: M.S. or M.A. in Social Work (or closely related field). Preferred Qualifications Current SW Licensure ( LMSW / LCSW ) or equivalent in related field. Previous graduate-level social work teaching experience. Prior exposure to supervising in a social work setting. Experience with Brightspace or other online learning management systems ( LMS ). Experience with other teaching technologies (e.g. Collaborate, Voicethread, Zoom, etc.) Experience with online instruction is preferred for candidates interested in teaching online. Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Competitive Additional Salary Information Job Type Varies Campus North Campus Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary For questions regarding the MSW program: Contact Name: Katie McClain-Meeder ( MSW Contact) Contact Title: Associate Professor, Director of the MSW Program Contact Phone/Extension: 716-645-1252 Contact Email: mcclainm@buffalo.edu For questions regarding the DSW program: Contact Name: Louanne Bakk ( DSW Contact) Contact Title: Clinical Associate Professor, DSW Program Director Contact Phone/Extension: 716-645-1861 Contact Email: louanneb@buffalo.edu For questions regarding the Undergraduate program: Contact Name: Filomena Critelli (Undergraduate Contact) Contact Title: Associate Professor, Director of Undergraduate Studies Contact Phone/Extension: 716-645-1250 Contact Email: fmc8@buffalo.edu Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Katie McClain-Meeder Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title MSW Program Director Contact's Email mcclainm@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-645-1260 Posting Dates Posted 07/07/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled References Number of References Required 2 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs * Please indicate your area of interest DSW Only MSW Only Undergraduate Only DWS & MSW DSW & Undergraduate MSW & Undergraduate All * Please indicate your semester availability. Fall/Spring Fall only Spring only Summer only All * Please indicate your subject area(s) of expertise and/or course interests. (For a list of course offerings, please visit the link listed in the position summary of the posting) (Open Ended Question) * Please specify your preferred teaching methodology. Seated instruction Online instruction Both * Are you a SUNY employee eligible for special consideration as a result of retrenchment? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65169": {"title": "Associate Dean for Academic Affairs, School of Nursing", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Associate Dean for Academic Affairs, School of Nursing Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Associate Dean for Academic Affairs, School of Nursing Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Associate Dean for Academic Affairs, School of Nursing Department School of Nursing Posting Number F260026 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/61587 Employer State Faculty Appointment Term Term Position Type UUP Faculty Bargaining Unit Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2025-2026 Position Summary The Associate Dean for Academic Affairs ( ADAA ) primary role is to support the School of Nursing\u2019s academic mission by providing leadership, oversight, and direction across undergraduate (BS, ABS , RN/BS) and graduate programs ( DNP and PhD). The School of Nursing is seeking a visionary leader who can inspire faculty, is a strategic thinker, engages with leadership and faculty across the University at Buffalo as the School positions itself for continued growth and expansion across our shared education, research, and practice/service missions. The ADAA builds, maintains, and sustains a collaborative working environment with the school\u2019s leadership team and fosters a community of faculty and student scholars that have a core commitment to academic excellence, high research productivity, and innovation in practice and community/professional service. The ADAA will continue to build and strengthen a core commitment to diversity, equity and inclusion to prepare the leaders of tomorrow for service to their local, regional, state, national and global communities. The School of Nursing and the University at Buffalo aspire to become one of the top 25 public institutions in the nation. The ADAA is a member of the Executive Leadership Team (Associate Dean for Academic Affairs ( ADAA ), Associate Dean for Research ( ADR ), Assistant/Associate Deans and Sr. Assistant Dean for Administration and Finance ( ADAF ) and reports directly to the Dean of the School of Nursing. The ADAA also provides oversight and direction to the Office of Student Affairs/Services, Simulation Services and Interprofessional Education efforts, the Educational Staff Service Support team and interfaces with accreditation and professional licensing entities, Information Technology Services that manages computer/audiovisual technology and the learning management system (Brightspace). Responsibilities: Academic Programs Provides overall leadership and implements the strategic vision across the undergraduate (BS, ABS , RN-BS) and graduate programs ( DNP and PhD) to ensure academic excellence and compliance of all programs with applicable accreditation and licensing requirements consistent with an R1 AAU research intensive university. Collaborates with Assistant/Associate Deans and Program Directors in the School of Nursing and Academic leaders across the university (Vice Provost for Graduate Education and Dean of the Graduate School etc.) regarding curriculum implementation, operational efficiency, and innovative academic programming. Recruits and retains highly qualified tenured/tenure-track, clinical track, and adjunct faculty to achieve excellent educational outcomes for students. Works with other Assistant/Associate Deans/Program Directors to assign and balance faculty workload to achieve educational, research, and practice/service goals. Works with the Dean and other members of the leadership team to plan, design, implement, and innovate new programs/course offerings for students, alumni, and community members. Monitor and work with the Dean, ADR , ADAF , and VP for Graduate Education/Dean of the Graduate School on the use and deployment of TA/GA/RA student appointments to meet strategic and financial goals. Develops, modifies, and maintains school and academic policies as needed to support educational objectives, achieve accreditation standards, and comply with licensing requirements. Works with faculty to obtain external funding from Health Resources and Services Administration ( HRSA ), or other components of the Department of Health and Human Services ( HHS ) to support innovative programmatic expansion and excellence in undergraduate and graduate programs ( DNP and PhD). Meet with other ADAA\u2019s and serve on the Associate Deans Councils across decanal units to advance the outcomes and innovate new programs, develop university wide policies, and share/disseminate information with members of the SON as appropriate. Engages with the Vice Provosts and Deans of the Graduate and Undergraduate Schools regarding curriculum, students, enrollment, faculty, and student issues as needed to achieve program outcomes. Enrollment Management Meets as needed as part of the enrollment management team to recruit and retain excellent students with attention to achieving the goals of holistic enrollment to ensure that the SON provides an equitable and inclusive environment for diverse students. Monitors student progress, retention, and completion across the programs. Tracks program metrics for graduation success, time to completion, outcomes and diversity. Accreditation and Licensing Reviews, monitors, and evaluates program performance to lead and meet implementation of accreditation standards across accrediting entities and licensing agencies. Provides leadership for accreditation, licensing, site visits, self-studies, and other required documents and activities as needed to meet, implement, and maintain SUNY , COA , CCNE , AACN , NY State Office of Professions standards/requirements and/or other accrediting bodies. Provides oversight regarding curriculum evaluation and implementation. Monitors student performance on state/national licensing exams for quality outcomes. Advising and Student Services Provides oversight to the Office of Student Affairs regarding advising and student services for pre-admitted/admitted students; out-of-state and international student recruitment and retention initiatives as appropriate; provides oversight for any issues that impact student success across programs including student progression, grade changes, grievances, double major requests, Academic Integrity, and student athletic team participation. Coordinate with the Office of Student Affairs to provide oversight of scholarships and awards to students consistent with SON and university policies. Faculty Development Provides oversight to ensure faculty development for junior/senior faculty to advance in the development of their teaching and classroom performance. Work with the Dean and Assistant/Associate Deans and Associate Dean for Research to develop and coordinate faculty mentoring to support faculty in pursuit of promotion in the tenure track and/or clinical ranks to achieve academic scholarship goals consistent with a R1/ AAU research intensive program/clinical scholarship to achieve promotion in rank with respect to their faculty appointment. Evaluation and Assessment Provides overall oversight and guidance for annual evaluation of courses, programs, faculty, students and staff to achieve educational and practice/service goals of the SON . Works with the ADR regarding faculty assessment for research and scholarship productivity. Technology, Simulation, and Learning Management System Provides oversight for simulation and IPE activities for undergraduate and graduate programs. Works with the information technology (IT) team and instructional designer regarding the use of computer and information systems to support operation of educational programs and delivery of the curriculum for in class/online activities regarding the use of software. Recommend securing and adaptation of new software, resources, and equipment to support effective delivery of the curriculum and services to advance the strategic goals of the SON . Practice and Community Partnerships Coordinate with the Dean and other academic unit leaders in nursing to facilitate and expand practice opportunities and community partnerships to support the academic, research and practice mission for students and faculty in the SON . Engage with practice and community partners to secure clinical placements and maintain academic-practice partnership relations. Performs other duties assigned by the Dean. We are particularly looking for candidates who can operate effectively in a diverse community of students and faculty and share our vision of helping all constituents reach their full potential. We are committed to developing an excellent and diverse community of scholars and students engaged in education, research, and service. We encourage applications from women, members of historically marginalized groups, veterans, and individuals with disabilities. About UB School of Nursing Founded in 1936, UB School of Nursing is a leader in high-quality nursing education and research in a dynamic university setting. Our mission continues our scholarly excellence as we educate clinical leaders, conduct impactful research, and deliver clinical care based upon principles of collaboration, equity, inclusion, and social justice for our region and the world. Our undergraduate programs prepare nurses for expanded professional roles in an increasingly complex and evolving health care environment, and our graduate and advanced certificate programs prepare clinicians, researchers, educators and leaders to provide complex care across settings, educate the next generation of nurses, and advance nursing and health care knowledge. Learn more: Our benefits , where we prioritize your well-being and success to enhance every aspect of your life. Being a part of the University at Buffalo community. The University at Buffalo is an equal opportunity employer ( EOE ) and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with a disability. Minimum Qualifications Earned doctorate ( DNP and/or PhD) in nursing with undergraduate/graduate degrees from regionally accredited colleges/universities. Registered nurse licensed (or license eligible) to practice in the State of New York. CV consistent to hold the rank of Associate Professor/Professor (clinical and/or tenure track) at the University at Buffalo and be a member of the Graduate Faculty. Evidence of a sustained and progressive record of academic leadership and scholarly productivity at the national level. Prior administrative, teaching, research and clinical practice experience involving the successful management of faculty, students and/or professional staff. Ability to lead in a complex organizational environment. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience as an Assistant/Associate Dean or Department chair in an Undergraduate and/or Graduate Program(s). Ability to organize, inspire, support, and build effective teams to advance the missions of the SON ; listen and build consensus among varied constituents; promote innovation and manage change; respond to and manage difficult conversations to achieve outcomes and improve the School of Nursing. Ability to work collaboratively and effectively with the Dean and SON leadership, faculty, staff, and students to advance UB\u2019s mission to become a top 25 public research university. Prior experience supporting and/or developing and implementing new academic programs. Experience developing and sustaining collaborative partnerships. Strong communication skills across students, faculty, staff, alumni, and community partners to achieve strategic outcomes. Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Competitive Additional Salary Information Job Type Full-Time Campus South Campus Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Jackie Martek Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title Senior Staff Assistant Contact's Email jmartek@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-829-3537 Posting Dates Posted 03/10/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled References Number of References Required 3 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a SUNY employee eligible for special consideration as a result of retrenchment? Yes No * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65168": {"title": "Assistant Clinical Professor, School of Law", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Assistant Clinical Professor, School of Law Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Assistant Clinical Professor, School of Law Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Clinical Professor, School of Law Department School of Law Posting Number F260071 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/63528 Employer State Faculty Appointment Term Term Position Type UUP Faculty Bargaining Unit 08 - UUP Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2026-2027 Position Summary The University at Buffalo School of Law invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure track assistant clinical professor to direct its Family Violence and Women\u2019s Right clinic, specifically in the areas of Domestic Violence and related Family Law. Three-year contract, indefinitely renewable if appropriate progress is achieved, with potential advancement to ranks of Associate Clinical Professor and Clinical Professor in subsequent contract terms. Position Responsibilities include: All aspects of teaching, supervising, and directing a Domestic Violence and Family Law Clinic, including curriculum development and maintaining an active clinical legal practice within the local community. Assisting with planning, drafting, applying for, and securing grants to support the clinic and clinical department. Managing grants and state funding, including internal oversight for deadlines, records, and reporting as well as monitoring federal, state, and local grants in accordance with applicable standards, regulations, and guidelines. Additional teaching obligations with an experiential focus. Service obligations related to the program as well as departmental and university affiliations. The University at Buffalo School of Law\u2019s Clinical Legal Education Program seeks to recruit and retain a diverse workforce as a reflection of our commitment to serve the diverse people of Buffalo, to maintain the excellence of the university and to offer our students richly varied disciplines, perspectives, and ways of knowing and learning. Learn more: Our benefits , where we prioritize your well-being and success to enhance every aspect of your life. Being a part of the University at Buffalo community. The University at Buffalo is an equal opportunity employer ( EOE ) and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with a disability. Minimum Qualifications J.D. degree and a minimum of three years legal practice experience in domestic violence and family law. Admitted to the practice of law in New York State or verifiable ability to gain admission by January 2027. Authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Must be able to work some nights and weekends. Must be able to engage in limited travel. Preferred Qualifications Five years of relevant legal experience. Law school or similar teaching experience. Demonstrated ability to work with individuals and groups from diverse backgrounds, cultures, and locations. Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range $110,000 - $120,000 Based on Experience Additional Salary Information Job Type Full-Time Campus North Campus Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Bernadette Gargano Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title Vice Dean/Director of Clinical Legal Education Contact's Email law-clinic@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716- 645-2167 Posting Dates Posted 07/21/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled 12/31/2026 References Number of References Required 3 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a SUNY employee eligible for special consideration as a result of retrenchment? Yes No * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Writing Sample Optional Documents Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65167": {"title": "Assistant Teaching Professor, Japanese Cultural Studies (Non-Tenure-Track)", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Assistant Teaching Professor, Japanese Cultural Studies (Non-Tenure-Track) Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Assistant Teaching Professor, Japanese Cultural Studies (Non-Tenure-Track) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Teaching Professor, Japanese Cultural Studies (Non-Tenure-Track) Department Asian Studies Program Posting Number F260102 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/64251 Employer State Faculty Appointment Term Term Position Type UUP Faculty Bargaining Unit 08 - UUP Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2026-2027 Position Summary The University at Buffalo, The State University of New York, invites applications for a 10 month full-time, non-tenure-track qualified rank teaching position in Japanese Cultural Studies. The appointment will be made in the Asian Studies Program in the College of Arts and Sciences. The position is designed for an educator whose primary professional commitment is undergraduate teaching, curriculum development, and student engagement, and who is interested in making a sustained contribution to this interdisciplinary program. The position requires teaching up to four interdisciplinary courses per semester in humanities and/or social sciences. The successful candidate will teach established undergraduate courses as well as develop new courses that contribute to the Asian Studies curriculum. A particularly important responsibility will be teaching large-enrollment courses on Japanese anime and popular culture. Other courses include, but are not limited to, a survey of Asian literature and a first-year seminar on Japan Studies. The position is especially well suited to a candidate with demonstrated success teaching Japanese anime, manga, film, media, and other forms of Japanese popular culture to undergraduates, including students from a wide range of disciplinary backgrounds. The Assistant Teaching Professor will be responsible for sustaining and expanding the program\u2019s undergraduate curriculum through effective, student-centered teaching and the development of new courses that prepare students for professional careers in Asia or with Asian businesses and communities. These courses could address topics such as Japanese media and popular culture, literature, history, urban societies, gender and sexuality, religion, politics, migration, labor, technology, food, and other subjects related to Asian Studies. We welcome candidates who can bring broad knowledge of Japanese culture to an interdisciplinary undergraduate curriculum and who are eager to develop courses that attract and serve students beyond the Asian Studies major. This is a teaching-focused position with no research or publication obligation. We seek a colleague who regards undergraduate teaching and curriculum development as the central focus of their professional work and who is interested in making a long-term contribution as a teaching-focused faculty member. The three-year term appointment (academic-year obligation) offers an opportunity to develop an important role in the Asian Studies Program through excellent teaching, student mentoring, curricular innovation, and service to the program. The university is especially interested in candidates whose experience in teaching or community service has prepared them to contribute to our commitment to diversity and excellence. Hiring will be for the spring 2027 semester. Candidates must have conferred a PhD in Asian Studies or a related field by the time of appointment and demonstrate experience and excellence teaching undergraduate courses in Japanese studies, cultural studies, or related fields. Particular consideration shall be given to candidates who have taught anime, popular culture, or related courses. Demonstrated success teaching large-enrollment undergraduate courses is strongly preferred. The candidate\u2019s disciplinary training may be in Japanese Studies, Asian Studies, cultural studies, media studies, literature, history, or another related field. Review of applications begins September 25, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. The following documents are required: Curriculum vitae A teaching portfolio which includes: a statement of teaching philosophy; two sample syllabi (including one for a course on Japanese anime); and a sample of course evaluations Cover letter : applicants should describe their experience teaching Japanese cultural studies to undergraduates, their experience with large-enrollment courses where applicable, and the ways in which their teaching and curricular interests would contribute to the Asian Studies Program at the University at Buffalo. All application materials should be submitted via UB Jobs at this link: https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/64251 . Application materials submitted directly to the posting contact will not be acknowledged and cannot be considered. Learn more: Our benefits , where we prioritize your well-being and success to enhance every aspect of your life. Being a part of the University at Buffalo community. The University at Buffalo is an equal opportunity employer ( EOE ) and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with a disability. Minimum Qualifications PhD in Asian Studies or a related field by the time of appointment Experience teaching undergraduate courses in Japanese studies, Japanese cultural studies, cultural studies, or a related field. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated success teaching courses on anime, Japanese popular culture, or related subjects Demonstrated success teaching large-enrollment courses. Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Competitive Additional Salary Information Job Type Full-Time Campus North Campus Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary Review of applications will begin September 25, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. The following documents are required: Curriculum vitae Teaching Portfolio Cover letter All application materials should be submitted via UB Jobs. Application materials submitted directly to the posting contact will not be acknowledged and cannot be considered. Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Walter Hakala Contact's Pronouns he/him/his Contact's Title Director, Asian Studies Program Contact's Email walterha@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-645-3419 Posting Dates Posted 09/10/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled 01/07/2027 References Number of References Required 3 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a SUNY employee eligible for special consideration as a result of retrenchment? Yes No * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Portfolio Optional Documents Optional Additional Document Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65166": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor, School of Nursing", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Adjunct Instructor, School of Nursing Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Adjunct Instructor, School of Nursing Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Adjunct Instructor, School of Nursing Department School of Nursing Posting Number F260069 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/63505 Employer State Faculty Appointment Term Temporary Position Type UUP Faculty Bargaining Unit Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2026-2027 Position Summary The University at Buffalo, School of Nursing is seeking exceptional part-time adjunct faculty who are dedicated to providing quality educational experiences and to teach in clinical settings for the undergraduate pre-licensure program. Teach Clinical courses are offered primarily Wednesdays through Saturdays. The position requires availability to teach in clinical settings approximately 12-16 hours per week. In this role, you will: Attend (in-person or virtually) meetings in the fall and spring semesters. Communicate effectively and respectfully. Maintain a strong commitment to Nursing\u2019s ethics and values as well as the school\u2019s mission and vision. Outstanding Benefits Package Working at UB comes with benefits that exceed salary alone. There are personal rewards including comprehensive health and retirement plan options. We also focus on creating and sustaining a healthy mix of work, personal and academic pursuit \u2013 all in an effort to support your work-life effectiveness. We support your growth and development through our career coaching and training department and we qualify as a public service loan forgiveness organization. Learn more about our benefit packages . About The University at Buffalo The University at Buffalo (UB) #ubuffalo is one of America\u2019s leading public research universities and a flagship of the State University of New York system, recognized for our excellence and our impact. UB is a premier, research-intensive public university dedicated to academic excellence. Our research, creative activity and people positively impact the world. Like the city we call home, UB is distinguished by a culture of resilient optimism, resourceful thinking and pragmatic dreaming that enables us to reach others every day. Visit our website to learn more about the University at Buffalo . The University at Buffalo is an equal opportunity employer ( EOE ) and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with a disability. Minimum Qualifications A Master\u2019s Degree in nursing and two years clinical experience are required. Current NYS Nurse Registered Professional (RN) License (at the time of hire). Preferred Qualifications Previous experience with one of the following: Pediatrics, maternal-child health, mental health, medical/surgical, and other acute care settings such as critical care, urgent care, orthopedics, telemetry, neurology, oncology, and long-term care. Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Competitive Additional Salary Information Job Type Part-Time Campus South Campus Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary All applicants must apply online through UB Jobs. Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Lynn Emminger Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title Assistant Director for HR/Facilities Contact's Email emmingly@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-829-6807 Posting Dates Posted 07/21/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled References Number of References Required 3 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a SUNY employee eligible for special consideration as a result of retrenchment? Yes No * What will be the highest level of education attained by the time of employment? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Masters Degree PhD/Doctoral Degree MD JD * Will you have a New York State RN license by the time of appointment? Yes No * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents Certifications Copy of NYS RN license Diplomas Transcripts Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65165": {"title": "Clinical Associate/Full Professor - Pediatric Surgery, Department of Surgery", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Clinical Associate/Full Professor - Pediatric Surgery, Department of Surgery Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Clinical Associate/Full Professor - Pediatric Surgery, Department of Surgery Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Clinical Associate/Full Professor - Pediatric Surgery, Department of Surgery Department Surgery Posting Number F260002 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/60608 Employer State Faculty Appointment Term Term Position Type UUP Faculty Bargaining Unit Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2025-2026 Position Summary The Department of Surgery within the Jacobs School of Medicine and Biomedical Sciences, State University of New York at Buffalo (UB), is seeking a highly qualified Pediatric Surgeon. This full-time position will be based at our major affiliated teaching hospitals, with an appointment at the Clinical Associate or Full Professor level. The successful candidate will play a vital role in advancing pediatric surgery services and will demonstrate a commitment to excellence in patient-centered care. Overall duties include: Serving as attending physician for inpatient pediatric care services Providing consultation, treatment, and follow-up for pediatric surgery patients Teaching and mentoring residents, fellows, and medical students Engaging in clinical and basic science research, as well as participating in clinical trials that promote advancements in pediatric surgery Learn more: Our benefits , where we prioritize your well-being and success to enhance every aspect of your life. Being a part of the University at Buffalo community. The University at Buffalo is an equal opportunity employer ( EOE ) and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with a disability. Minimum Qualifications Candidates must have a MD or equivalent degree and be Board Certified or Board Eligible in Pediatric Surgery. Fellowship training in Pediatric Surgery. Preferred Qualifications Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Competitive Additional Salary Information Job Type Varies Campus As Assigned Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Nargis Hossain Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title Contact's Email nhossain@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-859-7330 Posting Dates Posted 01/09/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled References Number of References Required 3 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs * Are you a SUNY employee eligible for special consideration as a result of retrenchment? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65164": {"title": "Instructor, Gifted Math", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Instructor, Gifted Math Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Instructor, Gifted Math Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Instructor, Gifted Math Department Gifted Math Program Posting Number F260054 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/62807 Employer State Faculty Appointment Term Temporary Position Type UUP Faculty Bargaining Unit Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2025-2026 Position Summary The University at Buffalo Gifted Math Program is looking for a part-time experienced mathematics teacher for an afterschool math class at a grade level in the range 7-12. The classes take place on Mondays and Wednesdays from 4 to 6:30 p.m. or from 6:30-9 p.m. They run from September through April. The Gifted Math Program works with 7th through 12th graders throughout Western New York who compete through rigorous testing to enter this program. Responsibilities include: Preparing and Teaching for 5 hours of class time per week. Differentiating instruction for a diverse group of students. Communicating with students, parents, and GMP staff by responding in a timely way to emails and phone calls. Attending staff meetings. Posting grades and assignments on UB Learns in a timely way or supervising instructional assistant in doing this. Helping us with student individual needs through feedback, phones calls home, and conferencing. Helping students who are absent due to illness or mandatory school activities to obtain missing work. Teachers of level 1 students participate in a new student orientation session. Teachers of level 2-4 students hold one Regents review session after classes have ended. Learn more: Our benefits , where we prioritize your well-being and success to enhance every aspect of your life. Being a part of the University at Buffalo community. About Western New York Western New York is an ideal place to live and work. Buffalo, called \u2019The City of Good Neighbors,\" offers outstanding public schools and affordable housing. Buffalo is a diverse cultural center with excellent theater, museums and music as well as sports teams. For more information, please see: Buffalo Niagara Region. The University at Buffalo is an equal opportunity employer ( EOE ) and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with a disability. Minimum Qualifications Bachelors degree in Mathematics or Mathematics Education NY state teacher\u2019s certification for 7 -12 mathematics Preferred Qualifications Masters degree in Mathematics Education Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Competitive Additional Salary Information Job Type Varies Campus As Assigned Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary Please note that while we are commencing our recruitment efforts for adjunct faculty positions, it is understood that hiring is contingent on course availability, funding and course enrollment. Interested candidates must apply through UB Jobs. Candidates invited to interview will be asked to provide two letters of reference, which address your exemplary teaching abilities. For questions regarding this posting, please email the contact listed above. Background check is required due to working with minor children Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? Yes Background Check Notification Employment in this position will be contingent on the university\u2019s verification of credentials and any other information required by federal or state law, and University at Buffalo policies, including the completion of a criminal history check. Contact Information Contact's Name Anne Izydorczak Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title Administrator, Gifted Math Program Contact's Email aemartin@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-645-4467 Posting Dates Posted 06/15/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled 08/17/2026 References Number of References Required 2 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant By providing the names and e-mail addresses of my references, I hereby authorize either Human Resources or the applicable hiring department to contact my references via e-mail to request a reference letter on my behalf. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What will be the highest level of education attained by the time of employment? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Masters Degree PhD/Doctoral Degree MD JD * Are you a SUNY employee eligible for special consideration as a result of retrenchment? Yes No * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65163": {"title": "Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor - Division of Genetics, Department of Pediatrics", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor - Division of Genetics, Department of Pediatrics Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor - Division of Genetics, Department of Pediatrics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor - Division of Genetics, Department of Pediatrics Department Pediatrics Posting Number F250071 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/57920 Employer State Faculty Appointment Term Term Position Type UUP Faculty Bargaining Unit Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2025-2026 Position Summary The Division of Genetics in the Department of Pediatrics, University at Buffalo (UB) Jacobs School of Medicine and Biomedical Sciences, and Oishei Children\u2019s Hospital is recruiting for a Clinical Geneticist . We are looking for a candidate who has experience in the area of general genetics/dysmorphology and is eager to help grow and support our regional genetics program. Duties/Responsibilities: Clinical duties will include inpatient consultation for children admitted to Oishei Children\u2019s Hospital and outpatient care in our pediatric multispecialty clinic in collaboration with a dietitian, nurse practitioner, PharmD and genetic counselors. The successful candidate will have experience in the evaluation, diagnosis, and management of children with genetic conditions and have a proven record of excellence in patient care in a family-centered environment. The successful applicant will be an academic physician who exhibits a balanced commitment to clinical care, education and/or scholarly activity. This position will offer teaching opportunities with protected time. We are seeking candidates with strong academic backgrounds who have an interest in being involved with the medical school genetics curriculum as well as involvement in the genetic counselor training program. Outstanding Benefits Package Working at UB comes with benefits that exceed salary alone. There are personal rewards including comprehensive health and retirement plan options. We also focus on creating and sustaining a healthy mix of work, personal and academic pursuit \u2013 all in an effort to support your work-life effectiveness. Visit our benefits website to learn about our benefit packages . About the Department The Division of Genetics runs an active outpatient clinic with a diverse patient population. Our providers also support the pediatric inpatient units, Maternal Fetal Medicine Center, Great Lakes Cancer Care, and several multidisciplinary clinics at Oishei Children\u2019s Hospital ( OCH ). We are part of the Regional New York State Newborn Screening Center ( NBS ) in Buffalo, New York. Oishei Children\u2019s Hospital and the Jacobs School of Medicine and Biomedical Sciences are located on the Buffalo Niagara Medical Campus ( BNMC ), a consortium of the region\u2019s premier health care, life sciences research and medical education institutes, all located on 120 acres in downtown Buffalo. This promotes strong interactions with the Clinical and Translational Research Center, the Institute for Healthcare Informatics and the New York State Center of Excellence for Bioinformatics and Life Sciences including the Buffalo Institute for Genomics and Data Analytics, Center for Computational Research and Hunter James Kelly Research Institute. This proximity provides outstanding collaborative opportunities in metabolism, genetics, genomics and bioinformatics. About The University at Buffalo The University at Buffalo (UB) #ubuffalo is one of America\u2019s leading public research universities and a flagship of the State University of New York system, recognized for our excellence and our impact. UB is a premier, research-intensive public university dedicated to academic excellence. Our research, creative activity and people positively impact the world. Like the city we call home, UB is distinguished by a culture of resilient optimism, resourceful thinking and pragmatic dreaming that enables us to reach others every day. Visit our website to learn more about the University at Buffalo . The University at Buffalo is an equal opportunity employer ( EOE ) and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with a disability. Minimum Qualifications MD, DO or equivalent degree Board certified/eligible in Pediatrics and Medical Genetics by ABMGG Preferred Qualifications Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Competitive Additional Salary Information Job Type Full-Time Campus Downtown Campus Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Linda Ramsey Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title Department Administrator Contact's Email lkramsey@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-323-0011 Posting Dates Posted 07/14/2025 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled References Number of References Required 1 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a SUNY employee eligible for special consideration as a result of retrenchment? Yes No * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65162": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor, School of Management", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Adjunct Instructor, School of Management Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Adjunct Instructor, School of Management Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Adjunct Instructor, School of Management Department MGT Deans Office Administration Posting Number F240162 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/54784 Employer State Faculty Appointment Term Temporary Position Type UUP Faculty Bargaining Unit Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2023-2024 Position Summary The School of Management at the University at Buffalo, the State University of New York ( SUNY ) offers a variety of part-time adjunct opportunities at the undergraduate and graduate level. We seek individuals who can understand and contribute to our mission and vision. Assignments include seated or on-line courses in a Business discipline of expertise. Essential Functions: Demonstrates appropriate knowledge of subject Provides students with appropriate learning materials and expertise in assigned subject(s) Evaluates students\u2019 performance and provide effective feedback to guide student learning and success. Responsible for contributing to and maintaining an inclusive and collaborative environment Since 1923, the UB School of Management has built an impressive reputation as one of the best schools of business in the world. The comprehensive range of our academic portfolio, the expertise of our faculty and the worldwide success of our graduates are the primary reasons for the school\u2019s acclaim. Learn more at mgt.buffalo.edu. This is a pooled posting, and positions are filled on an as-needed basis. About The University at Buffalo The University at Buffalo (UB) #ubuffalo is one of America\u2019s leading public research universities and a flagship of the State University of New York system, recognized for our excellence and our impact. UB is a premier, research-intensive public university dedicated to academic excellence. Our research, creative activity and people positively impact the world. Like the city we call home, UB is distinguished by a culture of resilient optimism, resourceful thinking and pragmatic dreaming that enables us to reach others every day. Visit our website to learn more about the University at Buffalo . The University at Buffalo is an equal opportunity employer ( EOE ) and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with a disability. Minimum Qualifications A bachelor\u2019s degree and (2) two years of experience in applicable discipline. Preferred Qualifications A master\u2019s degree with teaching experience in higher education and engagement in co-curricular activities with business school. Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Competitive Additional Salary Information Job Type Varies Campus As Assigned Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Erika Bagnoli Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title Unit Business Officer Contact's Email mgthr@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-645-4090 Posting Dates Posted 12/26/2024 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled References Number of References Required 1 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a SUNY employee eligible for special consideration as a result of retrenchment? Yes No * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65161": {"title": "Primary Care Accelerated Track (PCAT) Director", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Primary Care Accelerated Track (PCAT) Director Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Primary Care Accelerated Track (PCAT) Director Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Primary Care Accelerated Track (PCAT) Director Department JSMBS OME Curriculum Posting Number F260046 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/62358 Employer State Faculty Appointment Term Term Position Type UUP Faculty Bargaining Unit Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2025-2026 Position Summary The Office of Medical Curriculum is seeking an experienced physician-educator to serve as the Primary Care Accelerated Track ( PCAT ) Director , with concurrent appointment as Director of the IMC 501 PCAT Foundations Course and Director of the IMC 700 Longitudinal Integrated Clerkship/Longitudinal Clinical Experience ( LIC / LCE ). This 0.5 FTE leadership role provides academic, curricular, and operational oversight for the entire three-year accelerated primary care pathway, as outlined in the approved PCAT proposal. The PCAT Director serves as the single point of accountability for PCAT , overseeing governance, curriculum design, assessment, and continuous quality improvement across all PCAT elements, including admissions collaboration, foundational coursework, Health Sciences Scholarly Project integration, Clinical Immersions, longitudinal coaching, clinical experiences, the LIC / LCE , and transition to residency preparation. The Director ensures achievement of all competency-based outcomes and alignment with Medical Education Program Objectives (MEPOs), LCME accreditation requirements, and institutional standards. Key Responsibilities: Provide academic and administrative leadership for the Primary Care Accelerated Track ( PCAT ). Serve as Chair of the PCAT Governance Committee, which reports to the Curriculum Committee (CC). Serve concurrently as Director of the PCAT Foundations Course, and Director of the LIC / LCE ensuring coherence across these required elements. Ensure integration and alignment across all PCAT curricular components, including Foundations, HSSP , Clinical Immersions, longitudinal coaching, LIC / LCE , clinical experiences and transition to residency preparation. Ensure that PCAT students meet all clerkship learning objectives, Required Clinical Experiences, and competency-based outcomes through longitudinal and integrated curricular structures. Ensure alignment with Jacobs School MEPOs, Phase-level competencies, LCME standards, and institutional policies. Use backward design to develop, implement, and refine PCAT learning objectives, assessments, and instructional strategies appropriate for an accelerated pathway. Collaborate with the Office of Accreditation and Quality Improvement ( OAQI ) to define, monitor, and report PCAT -specific metrics and outcomes. Lead continuous program evaluation and quality improvement efforts across all PCAT components. Coordinate with Admissions to support PCAT recruitment, selection criteria, admissions processes, and pipeline alignment. Collaborate with HSSP leadership, Clinical Immersions directors, and LC coaches to ensure curricular coherence and aligned expectations. Work with clerkship directors and clinical departments to integrate discipline-specific objectives, assessments, and experiences within the PCAT structure. Oversee assessment practices to ensure fairness, consistency, transparency, and comparability with the traditional four-year curriculum. Serve as the primary point of contact for PCAT student concerns, feedback, and academic issues. Maintain curricular documentation and systems (UBLearns, MedHub, curriculum maps) in collaboration with OMC and educational technology staff. Learn more: Our benefits , where we prioritize your well-being and success to enhance every aspect of your life. Being a part of the University at Buffalo community. The University at Buffalo is an equal opportunity employer ( EOE ) and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with a disability. Minimum Qualifications MD, DO, or equivalent degree. Board certification in Internal Medicine, Family Medicine, or Pediatrics. Demonstrated experience in medical education leadership and curriculum design. Experience teaching, supervising, and assessing medical students in clinical learning environments. Strong organizational, leadership, and communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Experience directing or designing accelerated pathways, longitudinal curricula, or integrated medical education programs. Familiarity with LCME standards and requirements, curricular governance, and continuous quality improvement processes. Experience collaborating with admissions, assessment, quality improvement, or cross-phase curricular leadership teams. Experience working with longitudinal advising, coaching, or mentoring models. Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Competitive Additional Salary Information Job Type Varies Campus Downtown Campus Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Laura Willgohs Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title Administrative Director of Curricular Operations Contact's Email lauradom@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-829-5238 Posting Dates Posted 05/11/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled References Number of References Required 3 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a SUNY employee eligible for special consideration as a result of retrenchment? Yes No * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65160": {"title": "Clinical Assistant Professor/Clinical Associate Professor/Clinical Professor (HS) - Department of Restorative Dentistry", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Clinical Assistant Professor/Clinical Associate Professor/Clinical Professor (HS) - Department of Restorative Dentistry Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Clinical Assistant Professor/Clinical Associate Professor/Clinical Professor (HS) - Department of Restorative Dentistry Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Clinical Assistant Professor/Clinical Associate Professor/Clinical Professor (HS) - Department of Restorative Dentistry Department Department of Restorative Dentistry Posting Number F260094 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/64101 Employer State Faculty Appointment Term Term Position Type UUP Faculty Bargaining Unit 08 - UUP Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2026-2027 Position Summary The University at Buffalo School of Dental Medicine, Department of Restorative Dentistry , is presently conducting a search for full-time clinical faculty concentrating in Implant Dentistry. The Buhite-DiMino Center for Implant Dentistry seeks to promote inter-disciplinary education, advance clinical research and provide equal access to quality dental care to the community. The Center provides screenings, consultation, implant dentistry and oral health services. Major responsibilities include: Pre-clinical and clinical teaching of implant prosthodontics. Surgery at pre and post-doctoral level. Faculty rank commensurate with teaching experience and faculty practice opportunity is available for NYS licensed individuals. Learn more: Our benefits , where we prioritize your well-being and success to enhance every aspect of your life. Being a part of the University at Buffalo community. The University at Buffalo is an equal opportunity employer ( EOE ) and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with a disability. Minimum Qualifications DDS , DMD or equivalent degree Eligibility for licensure in New York State Preferred Qualifications A degree in Periodontics or Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery Post-Graduate training in approved program in Prosthodontics or Implant Dentistry Certificate Program. Previous teaching experience in Implant Dentistry Clinical Practice experience Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Commensurate with Experience and Opportunity for Faculty Practice Additional Salary Information Job Type Full-Time Campus South Campus Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? Yes Background Check Notification Employment in this position will be contingent on the university\u2019s verification of credentials and any other information required by federal or state law, and University at Buffalo policies, including the completion of a criminal history check. Contact Information Contact's Name Gina LaGreca Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title Program Coordinator Contact's Email ginalagr@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-829-2862 Posting Dates Posted 08/31/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled References Number of References Required 3 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status (e.g. H-1B visa status)? Yes No * Are you a SUNY employee eligible for special consideration as a result of retrenchment? Yes No * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65158": {"title": "Clinical Instructor, Registered Dental Hygienist", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Clinical Instructor, Registered Dental Hygienist Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Clinical Instructor, Registered Dental Hygienist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Clinical Instructor, Registered Dental Hygienist Department Department of Periodontics and Endodontics Posting Number F260091 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/64041 Employer State Faculty Appointment Term Term Position Type UUP Faculty Bargaining Unit 08 - UUP Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2026-2027 Position Summary The University at Buffalo\u2019s Department of Periodontics and Endodontics has played a pivotal role in training world-class clinicians, researchers and academicians who have now become leaders in dental education and research. The School of Dental Medicine is currently seeking a part-time Clinical Instructor with competency in Periodontics/Dental Hygiene. Responsibilities include: Provide periodontics instruction in preclinical and clinical courses to predoctoral education students. Provide consults for periodontal clinical cases. Provide clinic demonstrations. Learn more: Our benefits , where we prioritize your well-being and success to enhance every aspect of your life. Being a part of the University at Buffalo community. The University at Buffalo is an equal opportunity employer ( EOE ) and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with a disability. Minimum Qualifications Dental Hygiene Certificate, licensed in NY Preferred Qualifications Associate or Bachelor\u2019s Degree Prior experience teaching or research Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Competitive Additional Salary Information Job Type Part-Time Campus South Campus Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary Optional Documents for Application: Please attach your Dental Hygiene Certificate under Additional Supporting Documentation and your BLS Certificate under Additional Supporting Documentation 2 . Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? Yes Background Check Notification Employment in this position will be contingent on the university\u2019s verification of credentials and any other information required by federal or state law, and University at Buffalo policies, including the completion of a criminal history check. Contact Information Contact's Name Victoria Balazs Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title Program Coordinator Contact's Email vmbalazs@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-829-6643 Posting Dates Posted 08/26/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled References Number of References Required 3 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a SUNY employee eligible for special consideration as a result of retrenchment? Yes No * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents Additional Supporting Documentation Additional Supporting Documentation 2 Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65157": {"title": "Adjunct Field Educator/Field Liaison, Office of Educator Preparation", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Adjunct Field Educator/Field Liaison, Office of Educator Preparation Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Adjunct Field Educator/Field Liaison, Office of Educator Preparation Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Adjunct Field Educator/Field Liaison, Office of Educator Preparation Department Office of Educator Preparation Posting Number F260064 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/63366 Employer State Faculty Appointment Term Temporary Position Type UUP Faculty Bargaining Unit Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2026-2027 Position Summary The Graduate School of Education at The University at Buffalo, State University of New York ( SUNY ) is seeking individuals with experience and knowledge of teaching practices and school communities and the ability to make connections between the university teacher education curriculum and the skills and practice knowledge gained in resident field placements. The incumbent will work collaboratively with the Office of Educator Preparation to ensure quality residency experiences that enable students to meet required competencies and adhere to accreditation standards. Duties and Responsibilities (Field Educator): Provide on & off-site support to UB teacher residents during residency placement year. Provide regular feedback to teacher residents student to improve teaching skills & techniques. Provide ongoing informal and formal evaluation of resident progress. Submit three formal Student Teacher Assessment Record evaluations of resident performance. Actively coordinate and work with school liaisons in providing appropriate learning experiences for the residents. Conduct monthly small group class sessions with resident student teachers and provide in-depth support & learning. Duties and Responsibilities (Field Liaison): Make a minimum of one visit per month throughout the academic year (September \u2013 May) for each assigned resident. The visits should include a three-way meeting with the resident and mentor. Be available to problem-solve issues with the student and/or mentor teacher via phone or through additional field visits as needed; document any significant problems and the recommendations made to address the problem. Attend monthly meetings as required by the Office of Educator Preparation. Provide program feedback and evaluation as requested by the Office of Educator Preparation. Interview incoming candidates to ensure potential for success in a field placement. This is a 10-month position that runs August \u2013 May. This is a pooled posting, and positions are filled on an as-needed basis Learn more: Our benefits , where we prioritize your well-being and success to enhance every aspect of your life. Being a part of the University at Buffalo community. The University at Buffalo is an equal opportunity employer ( EOE ) and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with a disability. Minimum Qualifications Permanent / professional certification in NYS or the equivalent. Minimum of 3 years relevant teaching experience. Preferred Qualifications 7+ years of certified, K-12 classroom teaching experience in schools with diverse student populations. Urban teaching experience (required for funded programs with BPS ). Experience providing instructional coaching or mentoring. Demonstrated commitment to WNY school districts, families, and communities Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Competitive Additional Salary Information Job Type Part-Time Campus As Assigned Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary In your cover letter please indicate your applicable experience Teacher Education and/or Teaching experience This is a 10-month position that runs from August \u2013 May. Hiring is contingent on course availability, funding, and course enrollment. This is a pooled posting, and positions are filled on an as-needed basis. Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Dr. Elisabeth Etopio Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title Clinical Professor and Search Chair Contact's Email etopio@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-645-4034 Posting Dates Posted 07/14/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled References Number of References Required 2 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant By providing the names and e-mail addresses of my references, I hereby authorize either Human Resources or the applicable hiring department to contact my references via e-mail to request a reference letter on my behalf. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a SUNY employee eligible for special consideration as a result of retrenchment? Yes No * Do you hold permanent/professional certification in NYS or the equivalent for teaching? Yes No * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How many years of teaching experience do you have? 1 2 3 4 5+ * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65155": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor, School of Nursing", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Adjunct Instructor, School of Nursing Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Adjunct Instructor, School of Nursing Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Adjunct Instructor, School of Nursing Department School of Nursing Posting Number F260070 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/63506 Employer State Faculty Appointment Term Temporary Position Type UUP Faculty Bargaining Unit Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2026-2027 Position Summary The University at Buffalo, School of Nursing is seeking exceptional part-time adjunct faculty who are dedicated to providing quality educational experiences and to teach in clinical settings for the undergraduate pre-licensure program. Teach Clinical courses are offered primarily Wednesdays through Saturdays. The position requires availability to teach in clinical settings approximately 12-16 hours per week. In this role, you will: Attend (in-person or virtually) meetings in the fall and spring semesters. Communicate effectively and respectfully. Maintain a strong commitment to Nursing\u2019s ethics and values as well as the school\u2019s mission and vision. Outstanding Benefits Package Working at UB comes with benefits that exceed salary alone. There are personal rewards including comprehensive health and retirement plan options. We also focus on creating and sustaining a healthy mix of work, personal and academic pursuit \u2013 all in an effort to support your work-life effectiveness. We support your growth and development through our career coaching and training department and we qualify as a public service loan forgiveness organization. Learn more about our benefit packages . About The University at Buffalo The University at Buffalo (UB) #ubuffalo is one of America\u2019s leading public research universities and a flagship of the State University of New York system, recognized for our excellence and our impact. UB is a premier, research-intensive public university dedicated to academic excellence. Our research, creative activity and people positively impact the world. Like the city we call home, UB is distinguished by a culture of resilient optimism, resourceful thinking and pragmatic dreaming that enables us to reach others every day. Visit our website to learn more about the University at Buffalo . The University at Buffalo is an equal opportunity employer ( EOE ) and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with a disability. Minimum Qualifications A Bachelor\u2019s degree in Nursing and clinical experience are required. Enrolled in a Master\u2019s Degree program in Nursing. Current NYS Nurse Registered Professional (RN) License (at the time of hire). Preferred Qualifications Previous experience with one of the following: Pediatrics, maternal-child health, mental health, medical/surgical, and other acute care settings such as critical care, urgent care, orthopedics, telemetry, neurology, oncology, and long-term care. Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Ability to perform typical staff nurse duties in acute care settings. Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Competitive Additional Salary Information Job Type Part-Time Campus South Campus Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary All applicants must apply online through UB Jobs. Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Lynn Emminger Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title Assistant Director for HR/Facilities Contact's Email emmingly@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-829-6807 Posting Dates Posted 07/21/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled References Number of References Required 3 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a SUNY employee eligible for special consideration as a result of retrenchment? Yes No * What will be the highest level of education attained by the time of employment? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Masters Degree PhD/Doctoral Degree MD JD * Will you have a New York State RN license by the time of appointment? Yes No * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents Certifications Copy of NYS RN license Diplomas Transcripts Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65154": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Teaching (Lecturer 10 months)", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Assistant Professor of Teaching (Lecturer 10 months) Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Assistant Professor of Teaching (Lecturer 10 months) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Professor of Teaching (Lecturer 10 months) Department Computational & Data-Enabled Science & Engineering Posting Number F260000 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/60486 Employer State Faculty Appointment Term Term Position Type UUP Faculty Bargaining Unit Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2025-2026 Position Summary The Institute for Artificial Intelligence and Data Science ( IAD ) at the University at Buffalo (UB) invites applications for one Assistant Professor of Teaching position (Lecturer) in line with their experience and prior positions and offer competitive salaries. We are particularly looking for candidates who can operate effectively in a team environment and in a diverse community of students and faculty, and who share our vision of helping all constituents reach their full potential. Responsibilities and expectations are commensurate with rank and experience. The successful candidate will focus primarily on teaching and curriculum development within core courses of the data science programs. The faculty\u2019s primary duties are teaching Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, and Computational Science-related courses at the graduate level and advising these students. Other duties may include industry internship and student project supervision, experiential learning and student excellence initiatives; accreditation objectives; diversity enhancement; program administration, and external educational grant support. We are particularly interested in candidates with experience in and a passion for teaching courses in artificial intelligence, statistical learning, data mining, machine learning, database fundamentals, and related data models and queries. The IAD is the home of several graduate programs, including a Ph.D. in Computational and Data-Enabled Science and Engineering ( CDSE ), an MS in Engineering Science with Data Science focus ( ESDS ), an MS in Engineering Science with Artificial Intelligence focus ( ESAI ), an MS in Engineering Science with AI and Data Innovation focus, and a MPS in Data Science Applications ( DSA ). IAD coordinates interdisciplinary research including applications of data, computer, and computational sciences across various domains. The primary responsibility of the advertised positions is for the MS- ESDS program. Outstanding Benefits Package Working at UB comes with benefits that exceed salary alone. There are personal rewards including comprehensive health and retirement plan options. We also focus on creating and sustaining a healthy mix of work, personal and academic pursuit \u2013 all in an effort to support your work-life effectiveness. We support your growth and development through our career coaching and training department and we qualify as a public service loan forgiveness organization. Learn more about our benefit packages . About the University at Buffalo UB is a member of the prestigious Association of American Universities ( AAU ), and the largest and most comprehensive university in The State University of New York ( SUNY ) system, with about 22,000 undergraduates and 10,000 graduate and professional students and 1600 fulltime faculty. UB (together with Stony Brook University) is the official flagship university of SUNY and premier public institution in the Northeast. The School of Engineering and Applied Sciences has 7,300 students enrolled across 9 academic departments. About Buffalo Buffalo is the second-largest city in New York State and a hub connecting the East Coast and the Midwest. It features a rapidly growing economy, low cost-of-living, historic and eclectic neighborhoods, world-class art galleries and museums, a vibrant theater and music community, the Lake Erie waterfront, a city-wide system of parks designed by renowned landscape architect Frederick Law Olmsted, and major and minor league sports teams. The awe-inspiring Niagara Falls are just 20 minutes away. Buffalo is also a border city to Canada with direct access to the Toronto metro area. The IAD is located on UB\u2019s North Campus in suburban Amherst, an area known for its outstanding public schools and services. The University at Buffalo is an equal opportunity employer ( EOE ) and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with a disability. Minimum Qualifications Applicants should have a PhD degree in data science, computer science, computational sciences, applied mathematics, statistics, or a related field. Degree must be conferred prior to appointment. Preferred Qualifications Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Competitive Additional Salary Information Job Type Full-Time Campus North Campus Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary For Optional Additional Document, please attach an Educational Equity statement. Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Rachael Blair Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title IAD Associate Director Contact's Email hageman@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-821-8307 Posting Dates Posted 01/06/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled 09/01/2026 References Number of References Required 3 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a SUNY employee eligible for special consideration as a result of retrenchment? Yes No * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Teaching Statement Optional Documents Optional Additional Document Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65153": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor, Graduate School of Education", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Adjunct Instructor, Graduate School of Education Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Adjunct Instructor, Graduate School of Education Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Adjunct Instructor, Graduate School of Education Department Graduate School of Education Posting Number F260053 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/62765 Employer State Faculty Appointment Term Temporary Position Type UUP Faculty Bargaining Unit Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2025-2026 Position Summary We invite enthusiastic, forward thinkers to instruct, engage, and inspire students in the Graduate School of Education. Candidates should have the ability to teach a range of online and seated undergraduate and graduate level courses in the academic disciplines associated with our four departments: Counseling, School and Educational Psychology Educational Leadership and Policy Learning and Instruction Information Science Academic Responsibilities and Essential Functions: Deliver seated and/or online lessons to undergraduate and/or graduate students. Evaluate and grade student class work, assignments, papers, and/or quizzes/exams, providing effective feedback to guide student learning and success. Engage in the classroom, reply to emails/voicemails within 24 hours, and hold on campus/online office hours. Maintain knowledge in one\u2019s own discipline-related area by participating in professional development. Learn more: Our benefits , where we prioritize your well-being and success to enhance every aspect of your life. Being a part of the University at Buffalo community. The University at Buffalo is an equal opportunity employer ( EOE ) and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with a disability. Minimum Qualifications For teaching undergraduate courses: Bachelor\u2019s degree or equivalent in relevant discipline/field For teaching graduate and doctoral courses: Master\u2019s degree or equivalent in relevant discipline/field Preferred Qualifications Possess a Master\u2019s/PhD in education, counseling, or library and information science-related field, and one year experience with online and hybrid teaching and related methodologies. Be knowledgeable in multiple content areas and theoretical frameworks within stated discipline, as well as issues related to diversity and multiculturalism. Possess working knowledge of Brightspace, the learning management system at UB. Availability to work evening hours (for seated courses). Be recognized as exemplary instructor who has had evidence of reflective practice and experience working with diverse students. Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Competitive Additional Salary Information Job Type Varies Campus As Assigned Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary Please note that while we are commencing our recruitment efforts for adjunct faculty positions, it is understood that hiring is contingent on course availability, funding and course enrollment. Interested candidates must apply through UB Jobs. For questions regarding this posting, please email the contact listed above. Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Kristine Mariglia Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title Director of Personnel and Finance Contact's Email kmm74@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-645-1349 Posting Dates Posted 06/15/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled References Number of References Required 1 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant By providing the names and e-mail addresses of my references, I hereby authorize either Human Resources or the applicable hiring department to contact my references via e-mail to request a reference letter on my behalf. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is the highest level of education attained currently? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Masters Degree PHD MD J.D. * Please indicate your discipline/subject area of expertise. Elementary Education Secondary Education Higher Education K-12 School Leadership School Counseling Counselor Education Counseling Psychology School Psychology Rehabilitation Counseling Mental Health Counseling Librarianship/Information Education Other * If you selected \"Other\" for the previous question, please provide your discipline(s)/subject area(s) of expertise. (Open Ended Question) * Please specify your preferred teaching methodology. Seated instruction Online instruction Both * Please indicate your semester availability. Fall/Spring Fall only Spring only Summer only All * Are you a SUNY employee eligible for special consideration as a result of retrenchment? Yes No * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Teaching Statement Optional Documents Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65152": {"title": "Vice Chair for Research, Department of Psychiatry", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Vice Chair for Research, Department of Psychiatry Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Vice Chair for Research, Department of Psychiatry Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Vice Chair for Research, Department of Psychiatry Department Psychiatry Posting Number F250059 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/57614 Employer State Faculty Appointment Term Term Position Type UUP Faculty Bargaining Unit Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2024-2025 Position Summary The Department of Psychiatry at the Jacobs School of Medicine and Biomedical Sciences at the University at Buffalo is seeking a dynamic and innovative leader to join our team as the Vice Chair for Research (Associate or Full Professor). This position offers a unique opportunity to shape and advance the research mission of our department, which includes a group of dedicated researchers supported by a larger team of clinicians and educators committed to excellence in psychiatric care and education. In addition to maintaining their own research, the Vice Chair would mentor junior faculty and foster collaborative research initiatives within the department and with other behavioral and health sciences schools within the university and beyond. The Vice Chair would also work with Director of Clinical Trials and other research support staff to ensure an efficient and effective infrastructure for research that coordinates with existing research support within the medical school and the university. Innovation Promotion : Encourage and facilitate research innovation, addressing critical mental health challenges through interdisciplinary approaches. Partnership Development : Build and maintain collaborative partnerships with other institutions, organizations, and stakeholders to enhance research impact. Collaboration : Foster collaborative research initiatives with other behavioral and health departments within the institution and beyond. Research Oversight : Manage and oversee the department\u2019s research programs, ensuring high standards of scientific rigor and innovation. Grant Writing : Engage in, and lead, efforts to secure external research funding through competitive grant proposals. Staff Management : Recruit, train, and supervise research staff, promoting a supportive and productive research environment. The Vice Chair for Research should be an individual who has an established, independent research career in clinical and behavioral science and who has experience developing collaborative and multidisciplinary projects. The Vice Chair for Research should develop and maintain a broad knowledge of administrative, ethical and regulatory issues as it relates to research, with an emphasis on translational, and clinical and population relevant research. Outstanding Benefits Package Working at UB comes with benefits that exceed salary alone. There are personal rewards including comprehensive health and retirement plan options. We also focus on creating and sustaining a healthy mix of work, personal and academic pursuit \u2013 all in an effort to support your work-life effectiveness. We support your growth and development through our career coaching and training department and we qualify as a public service loan forgiveness organization. Learn more about our benefit packages . About the University at Buffalo (UB) UB is a State University of New York ( SUNY ) System flagship institution as a research-intensive institution and the largest, most comprehensive campus in the 64-campus SUNY System. UB comprises three campuses\u2014North Campus, South Campus and Downtown Campus\u2014and includes six health sciences schools (Jacobs School of Medicine and Biomedical Sciences, School of Public Health and Health Professions, School of Dental Medicine, School of Nursing, School of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences, and School of Social Work). About the School The Jacobs School of Medicine and Biomedical Sciences offers a unique consortium of affiliated teaching hospitals, health care systems, and freestanding ambulatory sites. These include Kaleida Health (4 hospitals), the world-renowned Roswell Park Comprehensive Cancer Center, Erie County Medical Center, Catholic Health (4 hospitals), the VA Western New York Healthcare System, community-based facilities, and smaller specialty clinicals. The UBMD Physicians Group is made up of >631 physicians, and 1,960 providers. Visit us at our website. About the Department The Department of Psychiatry is dedicated to advancing the understanding and treatment of psychiatric illnesses. Our 52 full-time and 89 volunteer faculty members, provide comprehensive mental health at numerous public and private facilities, serving adults, adolescents and children. These connections foster opportunities for innovative research projects. In addition to residents and fellows, we support a doctoral internship program accredited by the American Psychological Association with two tracks; 1) Developmental Approach to Mental Illness and 2) Substance Use and Mental Illness. Our faculty are known for their contributions to understanding family processes in psychiatric and medical disorders, alcohol and drug use, brain injury and recovery, domestic violence, medical ontology, pain management and a variety of clinical trials with adults and children. Emerging areas of research include eating disorders, neurodevelopmental disorders, forensic issues, patient treatment outcomes and psychiatric genetics. The University at Buffalo is an equal opportunity employer ( EOE ) and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with a disability. Minimum Qualifications PhD, MD, or equivalent in Psychiatry, Psychology, or a related field. Proven track record of securing external research funding in psychiatry or behavioral sciences aligned with psychiatry. Experience in managing research programs and successful mentoring of young researchers. Strong leadership and communication skills. Commitment to fostering collaborative and interdisciplinary research. Preferred Qualifications Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Competitive Additional Salary Information Job Type Varies Campus Erie County Medical Center Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Kathleen Benz Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title Psychiatry Department Administrator Contact's Email kbenz@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-898-5945 Posting Dates Posted 06/25/2025 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled References Number of References Required 3 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a SUNY employee eligible for special consideration as a result of retrenchment? Yes No * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65151": {"title": "Associate/Full Professor, Pharmaceutical Sciences", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Associate/Full Professor, Pharmaceutical Sciences Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Associate/Full Professor, Pharmaceutical Sciences Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Associate/Full Professor, Pharmaceutical Sciences Department Pharmaceutical Sciences Posting Number F260051 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/62412 Employer State Faculty Appointment Term Term Position Type UUP Faculty Bargaining Unit Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2025-2026 Position Summary The University at Buffalo (UB) School of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences ( SPPS ) is seeking a tenure track faculty member at the associate or full professor level to expand the UB Drug Discovery, Development, and Evaluation Hub ( DDDE ). This research hub provides leadership and creative approaches to support core innovations in drug discovery/development as well as the development of a translational therapeutic core to support clinical pharmacology, policy development and evaluative clinical sciences. Research specialty/focus areas: Medicinal and biological chemistry; quantitative computational chemistry and molecular modeling; target identification; AI/ML-based drug discovery. Rank Appointment in these positions will be at an academic rank commensurate with experience. Scholarship/Research Responsibilities: Faculty members will develop a sustainable, funded program of research in the relevant area of expertise. Collaborative scholarship is strongly encouraged among faculty colleagues within the school and across the university. Teaching Responsibilities: Faculty members will contribute to one or more of the school\u2019s degree programs (PharmD, Ph.D., MS, or BS) based on area of specialization and alignment with course delivery needs. Service Responsibilities: Service activities include service to the Department, School, and University (i.e., through active participation on committees), as agreed to with the Chair and Division Head (Drug and Biotherapeutic Discovery). Learn more: Our benefits , where we prioritize your well-being and success to enhance every aspect of your life. Being a part of the University at Buffalo community. The University at Buffalo is an equal opportunity employer ( EOE ) and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with a disability. Minimum Qualifications Ph.D., PharmD, or equivalent in appropriate field with relevant postdoctoral experience. Preferred Qualifications Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Commensurate with Experience Additional Salary Information Job Type Full-Time Campus South Campus Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary Review of applications will commence immediately and will continue until positions are filled. Please see our UB SPPS Drug Discovery, Development and Evaluation Hub Recruitment Web Page for further information on the DDDE Hub, our school, programs, university, and the Western New York area. We welcome you to join our journey in becoming a leading research hub in drug discovery, drug delivery and translational therapeutics. Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? Yes Background Check Notification Employment in this position will be contingent on the university\u2019s verification of credentials and any other information required by federal or state law, and University at Buffalo policies, including the completion of a criminal history check. Contact Information Contact's Name Rachel Poole Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title HR Specialist Contact's Email spps-hr@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-645-6042 Posting Dates Posted 06/02/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled References Number of References Required 3 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a SUNY employee eligible for special consideration as a result of retrenchment? Yes No * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65150": {"title": "Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor GFT - Department of Otolaryngology-Head and Neck Surgery", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor GFT - Department of Otolaryngology-Head and Neck Surgery Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor GFT - Department of Otolaryngology-Head and Neck Surgery Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor GFT - Department of Otolaryngology-Head and Neck Surgery Department Otolaryngology Posting Number F260092 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/64054 Employer State Faculty Appointment Term Term Position Type UUP Faculty Bargaining Unit 08 - UUP Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2026-2027 Position Summary The University at Buffalo Department of Otolaryngology \u2013Head & Neck Surgery is experiencing rapid growth under new leadership and is seeking outstanding otolaryngologists to join our expanding academic department. We welcome candidates with expertise in comprehensive otolaryngology or subspecialty practice, pediatric otolaryngology, otology/neurotology, laryngology, facial plastic and reconstructive surgery, sleep surgery, and related disciplines. Rank will commensurate with experience. Practice Highlights Referral base serving more than one million patients Practice opportunities across Erie County Medical Center and/or Kaleida Health High clinical demand with excellent opportunity for rapid practice growth Flexibility to develop a practice aligned with your interests and expertise Academic appointment at the Jacobs School of Medicine and Biomedical Sciences Competitive compensation with uncapped productivity incentives Responsibilities Provide outstanding patient care in general otolaryngology and/or your area of subspecialty expertise Develop and grow a high-quality clinical practice Participate in the education of medical students and residents Collaborate in multidisciplinary patient care Opportunities for research, innovation, and program development based on your interests Learn more: Our benefits , where we prioritize your well-being and success to enhance every aspect of your life. Being a part of the University at Buffalo community. The University at Buffalo is an equal opportunity employer ( EOE ) and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with a disability. Minimum Qualifications MD, DO, or equivalent degree Board-certified or board-eligible in Otolaryngology \u2013 Head & Neck Surgery Eligible for unrestricted New York State medical licensure Commitment to patient-centered care and collaboration Preferred Qualifications Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Competitive Additional Salary Information Job Type Varies Campus As Assigned Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Beverly Hurley Contact's Pronouns she/her/hers Contact's Title Department Executive Administrator Contact's Email bhurley@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-829-5536 Posting Dates Posted 08/27/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled 11/01/2026 References Number of References Required 3 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a SUNY employee eligible for special consideration as a result of retrenchment? Yes No * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65119": {"title": "Clinical Professor, Pediatric Pulmonologist", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Clinical Professor, Pediatric Pulmonologist Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Clinical Professor, Pediatric Pulmonologist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Clinical Professor, Pediatric Pulmonologist Department Pediatrics Posting Number F260112 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/64622 Employer State Faculty Appointment Term Term Position Type UUP Faculty Bargaining Unit 08 - UUP Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2026-2027 Position Summary The Department of Pediatrics in the Jacobs School of Medicine and Biomedical Sciences at the University at Buffalo (UB) is seeking a board-certified/board-eligible Pediatric Pulmonologist to join a dynamic and growing Division of Pediatric Pulmonology & Sleep Medicine. The selected candidate will contribute to clinical care, education, research, and program development, with significant leadership opportunities, including the potential to lead the Pediatric Cystic Fibrosis (CF) Program. Division & Program Highlights The Division provides comprehensive care for children with acute and chronic respiratory diseases, supported by a multidisciplinary team and strong institutional infrastructure. \u2022 Our multidisciplinary team includes physicians, nurse practitioners, respiratory therapists, research coordinators, a dietitian, and social worker \u2022 Advanced clinical capabilities \u2022 Flexible and rigid bronchoscopy, including interventional Pulmonary function testing \u2022 Sleep studies \u2022 High resolution CT \u2022 Genetic and molecular testing \u2022 Complex disease management \u2022 Home ventilation \u2022 Severe therapy resistant asthma (biologics, personalized treatment plans) \u2022 Chronic lung disease of prematurity \u2022 Rare interstitial lung diseases \u2022 Neuromuscular related respiratory failure \u2022 Pulmonary complications of systemic diseases \u2022 Advanced Therapeutic Interventions \u2022 Noninvasive ventilation \u2022 Mechanical ventilation management \u2022 Airway clearance therapies \u2022 Critical and Multidisciplinary Care \u2022 Co-management in Pediatric intensive care units \u2022 Coordination with cardiology, ENT , genetics and gastroenterology \u2022 Long-term care planning for medically complex children Cystic Fibrosis Program (Leadership Opportunity) Opportunity to lead and further develop a highly established Pediatric CF Center. \u2022 Accredited by the Cystic Fibrosis Foundation \u2022 Active participant in the Therapeutics Development Network ( TDN ) \u2022 Long-standing reputation as a high-performing CF center \u2022 Multidisciplinary care team with strong clinical and research infrastructure Leadership opportunities include program growth, clinical trials expansion, quality improvement, and regional/national collaboration. Clinical Responsibilities \u2022 Provide inpatient and outpatient pediatric pulmonology care \u2022 Participate in consult services ( PICU , NICU , general pediatrics) \u2022 Manage conditions such as cystic fibrosis, asthma, BPD , neuromuscular disease, and sleep disorders \u2022 Flexible bronchoscopy/advanced bronchoscopy \u2022 Participate in multidisciplinary clinics Academic & Research Opportunities \u2022 Faculty appointment with opportunities for protected academic time \u2022 Participation in clinical trials and outcomes research \u2022 Collaboration across pulmonary, allergy/immunology, neonatology, and critical care \u2022 Mentorship of trainees Teaching Responsibilities \u2022 Teach medical students, residents, and fellows \u2022 Participate in conferences and curriculum development \u2022 Leadership opportunities in fellowship education Practice Environment \u2022 UBMD Pediatrics \u2013 largest pediatric subspecialty group in Western New York \u2022 Affiliation with UBMD Physicians\u2019 Group \u2022 Strong administrative and operational support \u2022 State-of-the-art facilities at the only free-standing Children\u2019s Hospital in NY State Compensation & Benefits \u2022 Competitive salary \u2022 Retirement plan contributions \u2022 Health, dental, and vision insurance \u2022 Malpractice coverage \u2022 CME support \u2022 Our benefits, where we prioritize your well-being and success to enhance every aspect of your life. Why Buffalo? \u2022 Affordable housing and excellent schools \u2022 \u201cThe City of Good Neighbors\u201d \u2022 Commute-friendly \u2022 Family-friendly community \u2022 Four-season outdoor activities \u2022 Proximity to Toronto and major Northeast cities \u2022 Buffalo International Airport \u2022 Medical campus with Children\u2019s hospital, Cancer center, Adult Stroke center/Adult hospital and Medical School on site. \u2022 Click here to learn more UBMD Pediatrics is one of 16 practice plans within UBMD Physicians\u2019 Group, the single largest medical group in Western New York. We provide premier health care to infants, children, adolescents and adults. In addition to primary care pediatrics, we have 15 pediatric subspecialties. Our physicians make up the academic teaching faculty within the Department of Pediatrics at the Jacobs School of Medicine and Biomedical Sciences at the University at Buffalo and Golisano Children\u2019s Hospital. Learn more: Our benefits , where we prioritize your well-being and success to enhance every aspect of your life. Being a part of the University at Buffalo community. About the University at Buffalo The University at Buffalo (UB) #ubuffalo is one of America\u2019s leading public research universities and a flagship of the State University of New York system, recognized for our excellence and our impact. UB is a premier, research-intensive public university dedicated to academic excellence. Our research, creative activity and people positively impact the world. Like the city we call home, UB is distinguished by a culture of resilient optimism, resourceful thinking and pragmatic dreaming that enables us to reach others every day. Visit our website to learn more about the University at Buffalo . The successful applicant must share our unwavering commitment to excellence, integrity, collegiality, antiracism, and respect for the inclusion of individuals with diverse backgrounds. Minimum Qualifications \u2022 MD, DO, or equivalent degree \u2022 Board-certified/board-eligible in Pediatric Pulmonology \u2022 Eligible for New York State licensure \u2022 Interest in academic medicine Preferred Qualifications Leadership experience preferred for CF role Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Competitive Additional Salary Information The salary range reflects our good faith and reasonable estimate of the possible compensation at the time of posting, the role and associated responsibilities, and the experience, education, and training of the selected candidate. Job Type Full-Time Campus Downtown Campus Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Linda Ramsey Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title Department Administrator Contact's Email lkramsey@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-323-0011 Posting Dates Posted 10/06/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled References Number of References Required 1 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs * Are you a SUNY employee eligible for special consideration as a result of retrenchment? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65114": {"title": "Assistant Teaching Professor, Classics (non-tenure-track)", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Assistant Teaching Professor, Classics (non-tenure-track) Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Assistant Teaching Professor, Classics (non-tenure-track) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Teaching Professor, Classics (non-tenure-track) Department Classics Posting Number F260108 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/64474 Employer State Faculty Appointment Term Term Position Type UUP Faculty Bargaining Unit 08 - UUP Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2026-2027 Position Summary The Department of Classics at the University at Buffalo State University of New York invites applications for a non-tenure-track Assistant Teaching Professor (10-month obligation) in Archaeology and Cultural Heritage, with an anticipated start date of Spring 2027. The successful candidate will teach three courses per semester at the undergraduate and graduate levels and contribute to the department\u2019s programs in archaeology and cultural heritage. Teaching responsibilities may include courses in Greek archaeology, the archaeology of Magna Graecia, cultural heritage management, and broader introductory courses in archaeology and material culture. The position carries limited departmental service responsibilities. A Ph.D. in Classics, Archaeology, or a closely related field is required by the time of appointment. Candidates should have demonstrated experience in cultural heritage management and a research specialization in Greek archaeology, with expertise in Magna Graecia particularly welcome. University-level teaching experience is strongly preferred. The initial appointment term is for three years and is renewable, contingent upon satisfactory performance, departmental needs, and the availability of funding. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States by their start date. The University at Buffalo does not guarantee that it will sponsor, support, or otherwise assist with obtaining work authorization. About the University at Buffalo The University at Buffalo (UB) #ubuffalo is one of America\u2019s leading public research universities and a flagship of the State University of New York system, recognized for our excellence and our impact. UB is a premier, research-intensive public university dedicated to academic excellence. Our research, creative activity and people positively impact the world. Like the city we call home, UB is distinguished by a culture of resilient optimism, resourceful thinking and pragmatic dreaming that enables us to reach others every day. Visit our website to learn more about the University at Buffalo . Learn more: Our benefits , where we prioritize your well-being and success to enhance every aspect of your life. Being a part of the University at Buffalo community. University at Buffalo is an affirmative action/equal opportunity employer and, in keeping with our commitment, welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. in Classics, Archaeology, or closely related field Preferred Qualifications Expertise in Greek Archaeology and Cultural Heritage Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Competitive Additional Salary Information Job Type Full-Time Campus North Campus Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary Review of applications begins October 31, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Application materials require a full CV/resume and cover letter addressing how the applicant fits the criteria of the job, and previous student evaluations (if any). All application materials must be submitted via UB Jobs. Application materials submitted directly to the posting contact will not be acknowledged and cannot be considered. Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Becky O'Connor Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title Department Administrator Contact's Email baa4@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-645-0468 Posting Dates Posted 09/28/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled 08/16/2027 References Number of References Required 3 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs * Are you a SUNY employee eligible for special consideration as a result of retrenchment? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter CV/Resume Optional Documents Teaching Evaluations Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65107": {"title": "Associate or Full Professor of Empire Innovation, Sustainable Materials Chemistry", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Associate or Full Professor of Empire Innovation, Sustainable Materials Chemistry Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Associate or Full Professor of Empire Innovation, Sustainable Materials Chemistry Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Associate or Full Professor of Empire Innovation, Sustainable Materials Chemistry Department Department of Chemistry Posting Number F260104 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/64368 Employer State Faculty Appointment Term Term Position Type UUP Faculty Bargaining Unit 08 - UUP Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2026-2027 Position Summary The Department of Chemistry at the University at Buffalo, The State University of New York, invites applications for a SUNY Empire Innovation Program faculty position in sustainable materials chemistry, as broadly defined, at the level of Associate or Full Professor . Candidates with research interests in experimental chemistry \u2013 involving materials synthesis, characterization, measurement, and/or the development of analytical tools and methods \u2013 that advances sustainable technologies, energy conversion and storage, and a cleaner environment, are especially encouraged to apply. Research programs that integrate the development of functional materials with innovative approaches for their chemical, electrochemical, or spectroscopic characterization are particularly welcome. This position is supported by SUNY\u2019s Empire Innovation Program that funds the expansion of research excellence in strategic areas through the recruitment of top faculty that are recognized leaders of their fields. The successful candidate will be expected to Develop and sustain a nationally and internationally recognized, externally funded research program; Contribute to excellence in undergraduate and graduate education; Mentor students and researchers from diverse backgrounds; Provide leadership and service to the Department, University, and broader scientific community. Application materials must be submitted via UB Jobs at https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/64368 . Applications received by December 1, 2026 will be given priority consideration. The search will continue until the position is filled. About the Departmen t The Department of Chemistry offers a highly collaborative and research-intensive environment spanning the traditional areas of analytical, inorganic, organic, and physical chemistry, as well as interdisciplinary research at the interfaces of chemistry with materials science, engineering, biology, medicine, and physics. The Department is committed to excellence in research and education and to fostering an inclusive environment for students, faculty, and staff. Faculty benefit from extensive opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration across the University at Buffalo, including the College of Arts and Sciences; the Schools of Engineering and Applied Sciences, Dental Medicine, Medicine and Biomedical Sciences, and Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences; the RENEW Institute; and the Center for Computational Research, as well as with regional research partners including Roswell Park Comprehensive Cancer Center and the Hauptman-Woodward Medical Research Institute. About the University at Buffalo The University at Buffalo (UB) #ubuffalo is one of America\u2019s leading public research universities and a flagship of the State University of New York system, recognized for our excellence and our impact. UB is a premier, research-intensive public university dedicated to academic excellence. Our research, creative activity and people positively impact the world. Like the city we call home, UB is distinguished by a culture of resilient optimism, resourceful thinking and pragmatic dreaming that enables us to reach others every day. Visit our website to learn more about the University at Buffalo . Learn more: Our benefits , where we prioritize your well-being and success to enhance every aspect of your life. Being a part of the University at Buffalo community. University at Buffalo is an affirmative action/equal opportunity employer and, in keeping with our commitment, welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Minimum Qualifications - PhD in chemistry or related area and an active record of publications and presentations at scientific conferences. - The candidate is expected to be dedicated to undergraduate and graduate education. Preferred Qualifications Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Competitive Additional Salary Information Job Type Full-Time Campus North Campus Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary Applications received by December 1, 2026 will be given priority consideration. The search will continue until the position is filled. All application materials must be submitted via UB Jobs. Application materials submitted directly to the posting contact will not be acknowledged and cannot be considered. Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name David Watson Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title Professor Contact's Email dwatson3@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-645-4189 Posting Dates Posted 09/21/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled 08/16/2027 References Number of References Required 3 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs * Are you a SUNY employee eligible for special consideration as a result of retrenchment? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Research Statement Optional Documents Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65102": {"title": "Academic Scholar - Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor \u2013 Breast Surgery", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Academic Scholar - Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor \u2013 Breast Surgery Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Academic Scholar - Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor \u2013 Breast Surgery Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Fiscal Year 2026-2027 Position Title Academic Scholar - Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor \u2013 Breast Surgery Posting Category Faculty Department Surgery Posting Number U260083 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/64375 Employer University Affiliates Appointment Term Position Type Posting Detail Information Position Summary The Department of Surgery within the Jacobs School of Medicine and Biomedical Sciences, State University of New York at Buffalo (UB), is seeking a highly qualified Breast Surgeon with a commitment to serving underrepresented and minority populations. This position will be based at our major affiliated teaching hospitals, with an appointment at the Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor level. Rank will commensurate with experience. The successful candidate will play a vital role in advancing equitable healthcare access and will demonstrate a passion for providing culturally sensitive, patient-centered care for diverse communities. Overall duties include: Serving as attending physician for inpatient breast surgery services Providing consultation, treatment, and follow-up for patients with a focus on addressing the unique healthcare needs of underserved populations Teaching and mentoring residents, fellows, and medical students with an emphasis on cultural competency and inclusivity Engaging in clinical and basic science research, as well as participating in clinical trials that promote advancements in breast surgery and health equity Learn more: Our benefits , where we prioritize your well-being and success to enhance every aspect of your life. University at Buffalo is an affirmative action/equal opportunity employer and, in keeping with our commitment, welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Minimum Qualifications MD, DO, or equivalent degree Board Certified or Board Eligible in Breast Surgery Fellowship training in Breast/Oncologic Surgery. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range $0.00 Additional Salary Information The salary range reflects our good faith and reasonable estimate of the possible compensation at the time of posting, the role and associated responsibilities, and the experience, education, and training of the selected candidate. Job Type Varies Campus As Assigned Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Nargis Hossain Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title Academic Programs Officer Contact's Email nhossain@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-859-7330 Posting Dates Posted 09/17/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled References Number of References Required 3 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65094": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor, School of Law", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Adjunct Instructor, School of Law Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Adjunct Instructor, School of Law Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Adjunct Instructor, School of Law Department School of Law Posting Number F260093 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/64102 Employer State Faculty Appointment Term Term Position Type UUP Faculty Bargaining Unit 08 - UUP Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2026-2027 Position Summary The University at Buffalo School of Law welcomes applications for part-time Adjunct Instructor positions at the graduate and undergraduate level. As the only law school in the State University of New York ( SUNY ) system, the School of Law has a long tradition of leadership and excellence in interdisciplinary studies, public service, and innovative scholarship, teaching, and clinical education. Our adjunct faculty roster includes several current and former judges and other leading members of the Western New York bar. We seek similarly accomplished judges and attorneys who have demonstrated expertise in the subjects they wish to teach and are committed to providing quality educational experiences to our students. Essential duties include: Developing a syllabus and assessing student performance against learning outcomes; Providing students with appropriate materials and expertise in the assigned subjects; Contributing to and maintaining an inclusive and collaborative learning environment; Ensuring that students receive prompt and productive feedback concerning their work; and Attending adjunct faculty meetings in the fall and spring semesters. This is a pooled posting, and positions are filled on an as needed basis. About The University at Buffalo The University at Buffalo (UB) #ubuffalo is one of America\u2019s leading public research universities and a flagship of the State University of New York system, recognized for our excellence and our impact. UB is a premier, research-intensive public university dedicated to academic excellence. Our research, creative activity and people positively impact the world. Like the city we call home, UB is distinguished by a culture of resilient optimism, resourceful thinking and pragmatic dreaming that enables us to reach others every day. Visit our website to learn more about the University at Buffalo. University at Buffalo is an affirmative action/equal opportunity employer and, in keeping with our commitment, welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Minimum Qualifications J.D. or equivalent degree. Two or more years of professional legal experience. Preferred Qualifications A demonstrated history of successful teaching at the graduate or undergraduate level. A record of engagement with the School of Law. One or more advanced degrees in addition to the J.D. A judicial clerkship, judicial staff attorney, or similar experience. Supervisory experience in a legal practice setting. Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Competitive Additional Salary Information Job Type Varies Campus North Campus Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary Please submit a resume and cover letter. In your cover letter, please describe any applicable teaching experience in higher education. Hiring is contingent on course availability, funding, and course enrollment. Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Tess Calvert Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title Assistant Director of Personnel and Finance Contact's Email tesscalv@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-645-6624 Posting Dates Posted 08/31/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled References Number of References Required 1 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs * Are you a SUNY employee eligible for special consideration as a result of retrenchment? Yes No * Please select your subject area of interest. If you have additional subject areas of interest, please list them in the next question to follow. Alternative Dispute Resolution Business Associations/Corporations/Agency Civil Litigation and Procedure Commercial Law (UCC Courses) Commercial Litigation Corporate Finance and Securities Law