oyment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Prosthodontics Program Director Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Prosthodontics Program Director Department Department of Restorative Dentistry Posting Number F260068 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/63484 Employer State Faculty Appointment Term Term Position Type UUP Faculty Bargaining Unit 08 - UUP Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2026-2027 Position Summary The Restorative Dentistry Department is looking for experienced candidates to apply to a full-time clinical-track Associate Professor /Professor faculty position and serve as Program Director for the Prosthodontics residency program. The incumbent will be required to provide instruction in the preclinical and clinical courses for Advanced Education in Prosthodontics. Cross discipline clinical and didactic teaching within Restorative Dentistry with emphasis in oral rehabilitation and implant dentistry and participation in research and service activities. Faculty practice opportunity is available. The University at Buffalo is SUNY\u2019s most comprehensive public research university, and an outstanding place to work. UB amplifies ambition for faculty and staff by offering endless possibilities to achieve more. Here, people from all backgrounds and cultures challenge and inspire each other to discover, learn, and succeed. Dedicated staff and engaged faculty collaborate to further knowledge and understanding and develop tenacious graduates who are valued for their talents and their impact on global society. Visit our website to learn more about the Learn more: Our benefits , where we prioritize your well-being and success to enhance every aspect of your life. Being a part of the University at Buffalo community. Minimum Qualifications \u2022 DDS , DMD or equivalent \u2022 Board certified in Prosthodontics \u2022 Must have completed a formal accredited postgraduate program \u2022 Eligible for NY State Dental License \u2022 Must have a record of scholarship Preferred Qualifications \u2022 Advanced dental lab experience desirable \u2022 Experience in an academic institution in training dental students and/or residents \u2022 Clinical prosthodontic practice experience Prodig+ Executive Position Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Commensurate with Experience Additional Salary Information Job Type Full-Time Campus South Campus Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? Yes Background Check Notification For non-internal applicants: a selected candidate will have to complete and pass a background check prior to appointment. Contact Information Contact's Name Gina LaGreca Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title Program Coordinator Contact's Email ginalagr@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-829-2862 Posting Dates Posted 07/17/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled References Number of References Required 3 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs * Are you a SUNY employee eligible for special consideration as a result of retrenchment? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65065": {"title": "Academic Scholar- Pediatric Pulmonologist; Clinical Assistant/Associate/Full Professor", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Academic Scholar- Pediatric Pulmonologist; Clinical Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Academic Scholar- Pediatric Pulmonologist; Clinical Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Fiscal Year 2025-2026 Position Title Academic Scholar- Pediatric Pulmonologist; Clinical Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Posting Category Faculty Department Pediatrics Posting Number U260039 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/62337 Employer University Affiliates Appointment Term Position Type Posting Detail Information Position Summary The Department of Pediatrics in the Jacobs School of Medicine and Biomedical Sciences at the University at Buffalo (UB) is seeking a board-certified/board-eligible Pediatric Pulmonologist to join a dynamic and growing Division of Pediatric Pulmonology & Sleep Medicine. This is an academic faculty position at the Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor level, commensurate with experience and academic accomplishments. The selected candidate will contribute to clinical care, education, research, and program development, with significant leadership opportunities, including the potential to lead the Pediatric Cystic Fibrosis (CF) Program. Division & Program Highlights The Division provides comprehensive care for children with acute and chronic respiratory diseases, supported by a multidisciplinary team and strong institutional infrastructure. Our multidisciplinary team includes physicians, nurse practitioners, respiratory therapists, research coordinators, a dietitian, and social worker Advanced clinical capabilities Flexible and rigid bronchoscopy, including interventional Pulmonary function testing Sleep studies High resolution CT Genetic and molecular testing Complex disease management Home ventilation Severe therapy resistant asthma (biologics, personalized treatment plans) Chronic lung disease of prematurity Rare interstitial lung diseases Neuromuscular related respiratory failure Pulmonary complications of systemic diseases Advanced Therapeutic Interventions Noninvasive ventilation Mechanical ventilation management Airway clearance therapies Critical and Multidisciplinary Care Co-management in Pediatric intensive care units Coordination with cardiology, ENT , genetics and gastroenterology Long-term care planning for medically complex children Cystic Fibrosis Program (Leadership Opportunity) Opportunity to lead and further develop a highly established Pediatric CF Center. Accredited by the Cystic Fibrosis Foundation Active participant in the Therapeutics Development Network ( TDN ) Long-standing reputation as a high-performing CF center Multidisciplinary care team with strong clinical and research infrastructure Leadership opportunities include program growth, clinical trials expansion, quality improvement, and regional/national collaboration. Clinical Responsibilities Provide inpatient and outpatient pediatric pulmonology care Participate in consult services ( PICU , NICU , general pediatrics) Manage conditions such as cystic fibrosis, asthma, BPD , neuromuscular disease, and sleep disorders Flexible bronchoscopy/advanced bronchoscopy Participate in multidisciplinary clinics Academic & Research Opportunities Faculty appointment with opportunities for protected academic time Participation in clinical trials and outcomes research Collaboration across pulmonary, allergy/immunology, neonatology, and critical care Mentorship of trainees Teaching Responsibilities \u2022 Teach medical students, residents, and fellows \u2022 Participate in conferences and curriculum development \u2022 Leadership opportunities in fellowship education Practice Environment UBMD Pediatrics \u2013 largest pediatric subspecialty group in Western New York Affiliation with UBMD Physicians\u2019 Group Strong administrative and operational support State-of-the-art facilities at the only free-standing Children\u2019s Hospital in NY State Compensation & Benefits Competitive salary Retirement plan contributions, no employee contribution required Health, dental, and vision insurance Malpractice coverage CME support Why Buffalo? Affordable housing and excellent schools \u201cThe City of Good Neighbors\u201d Commute-friendly Family-friendly community Four-season outdoor activities Proximity to Toronto and major Northeast cities Buffalo International Airport Medical campus with Children\u2019s hospital, Cancer center, Adult Stroke center/Adult hospital and Medical School on site. Visit our Beautiful Buffalo Niagara page to learn more. UBMD Pediatrics is one of 16 practice plans within UBMD Physicians\u2019 Group, the single largest medical group in Western New York. We provide premier health care to infants, children, adolescents and adults. In addition to primary care pediatrics, we have 15 pediatric subspecialties. Our physicians make up the academic teaching faculty within the Department of Pediatrics at the Jacobs School of Medicine and Biomedical Sciences at the University at Buffalo and Golisano Children\u2019s Hospital. About The University at Buffalo The University at Buffalo (UB) #ubuffalo is one of America\u2019s leading public research universities and the largest, most comprehensive institution in the 64-campus State University of New York ( SUNY ) system, and a member institution of the prestigious Association of American Universities ( AAU ). Over 30,000 undergraduate, masters and doctoral students are enrolled at UB across 13 colleges/schools. Visit our website to learn more about the University at Buffalo. The successful applicant must share our unwavering commitment to excellence, integrity, collegiality, antiracism, and respect for the inclusion of individuals with diverse backgrounds. University at Buffalo is an affirmative action/equal opportunity employer and, in keeping with our commitment, welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Minimum Qualifications MD, DO, or equivalent degree Board-certified/board-eligible in Pediatric Pulmonology Eligible for New York State licensure Interest in academic medicine Preferred Qualifications Leadership experience preferred for CF role Physical Demands Driving Requirements Salary Range $0.00 Additional Salary Information The salary range reflects our good faith and reasonable estimate of the possible compensation at the time of posting, the role and associated responsibilities, and the experience, education, and training of the selected candidate. Job Type Full-Time Campus Downtown Campus Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary Documents Information: Letter of Interest - including leadership interest in CF program if applicable. Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Linda Ramsey Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title Department Administrator Contact's Email lkramsey@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-323-0011 Posting Dates Posted 05/12/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled References Number of References Required 3 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Letter of Interest Optional Documents Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65063": {"title": "Tenure-Track Assistant Professor Department of Information Science", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Tenure-Track Assistant Professor Department of Information Science Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Tenure-Track Assistant Professor Department of Information Science Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Tenure-Track Assistant Professor Department of Information Science Department Information Science Posting Number F260055 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/62915 Employer State Faculty Appointment Term Term Position Type UUP Faculty Bargaining Unit Posting Detail Information Fiscal Year 2025-2026 Position Summary The Department of Information Science in the Graduate School of Education , University at Buffalo, the State University of New York ( SUNY ) invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position to start in August 2027. We are a collaborative and collegial department that values research excellence, innovative teaching, inclusivity, and belonging. We currently offer an ALA -accredited MS in Information and Library Science, an MS in School Librarianship, an Advanced Studies Certificate, and a PhD in Information Science. We have collaborative agreements with the School of Law and the Department of Music for joint master\u2019s degrees and with the Department of English and the Department of History for combined BA/MS-SL degrees, as well as an anticipated undergraduate major in information science. We welcome candidates from any area of expertise, with particular interest in those working in socio-technical policy and ethics, HCI /human-AI interaction, information practices, cultural heritage informatics, or theory development in information science. Responsibilities include: Maintaining an active and productive research agenda commensurate with a Research 1 tenure-track faculty appointment Seeking external grant funding Teaching a total of four courses each year Advising Information Science doctoral, master\u2019s, and undergraduate students Participating in professional activities and serving on department, school, and university committees Appointments are for a ten-month academic year beginning the Fall of 2027. The Search Committee will accept applications until the position is filled. For best consideration, please submit your materials by September 15th, 2026 Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States by their start date. The University at Buffalo does not guarantee that it will sponsor, support, or otherwise assist with obtaining work authorization. The University at Buffalo is the most comprehensive university and one of two officially designated flagship institutions in the SUNY system. UB is a member of the Association of American Universities ( AAU ). Recently, US News and World Report ranked UB among the top 50 of the best public national universities. UB has also been named one of the \u201cGreat Colleges to Work For\u201d by the Chronicle of Higher Education. The Department of Information Science is ranked 24th in the 2026 US News & World Report Rankings for Library and Information Studies programs. Being a part of the University at Buffalo community. University at Buffalo is an affirmative action/equal opportunity employer and, in keeping with our commitment, welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Learn more: Our benefits , where we prioritize your well-being and success to enhance every aspect of your life. Being a part of the University at Buffalo community. The Search Committee will accept applications until the position is filled. For best consideration, please submit your materials by September 15th, 2026 Minimum Qualifications A doctorate degree at the time of appointment in Information Science, or a related field. Preferred Qualifications Research agenda with potential for acquiring external funding Published research or scholarship Online teaching experience at the graduate or undergraduate level or interest Experience or interest in multidisciplinary collaboration Experience working effectively with minoritized students Prodig+ No Executive Position No Physical Demands Driving Requirements This position will never drive a university owned vehicle. Salary Range Competitive Additional Salary Information Job Type Full-Time Campus South Campus Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary A cover letter that includes (s) a description of your relevant qualifications for the position and (b) a statement describing your research/scholarship and teaching experiences A Curriculum Vitae A sample publication or other demonstrations of research productivity Additional Information Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Dr. Amy VanScoy Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title Professor and Search Committee Chair Contact's Email vanscoy@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-645-1487 Posting Dates Posted 07/01/2026 Deadline for Applicants Date to be filled References Number of References Required 3 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions to Applicant Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate your current employment affiliation with the University at Buffalo. Faculty Faculty Student Association (FSA) Research Foundation Employee State Classified State Professional UB Foundation TA/GA Student No Current Employment Affiliation * How did you first hear about this employment opportunity? AcademicKeys.com CareerExposure.com CareerWomen.com Chronicle of Higher Education DiversitySearch.com GoogleJobs.com HERCjobs.org HigherEdJobs.com IMDiversity.com Indeed.com LinkedIn.com MBACareers.com Conference Personal Referral UBJobs.buffalo.edu Other WNY Jobs * Are you a SUNY employee eligible for special consideration as a result of retrenchment? Yes No * What will be the highest level of education attained by the time of employment? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Masters Degree PhD/Doctoral Degree MD JD Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Sample Publication Optional Documents Human Resources Townsend Hall 205 Hayes Rd Buffalo, NY 14214 716-645-7777 ub-hr@buffalo.edu UB is an AA/EOE and welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Arrangements will be made if an applicant has a disability in order to provide access to the application, interview and selection process upon request. Reasonable accommodation requests must be made in a timely manner by email at diversity@buffalo.edu or by phone 716-645-2266. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/65061": {"title": "Academic Scholar, Child Abuse Physician - Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor; Department of Pediatrics", "description": "University at Buffalo Portal | Academic Scholar, Child Abuse Physician - Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor; Department of Pediatrics Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Campus Maps Directory Labor Condition Applications University Non-Discrimination Statement Workplace and Employment Rights for Applicants and Employees Academic Scholar, Child Abuse Physician - Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor; Department of Pediatrics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Fiscal Year 2025-2026 Position Title Academic Scholar, Child Abuse Physician - Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor; Department of Pediatrics Posting Category Faculty Department Pediatrics Posting Number U260046 Posting Link https://www.ubjobs.buffalo.edu/postings/62677 Employer University Affiliates Appointment Term Position Type Posting Detail Information Position Summary The Department of Pediatrics , University at Buffalo (UB), Jacobs School of Medicine and Biomedical Sciences and Kaleida Health\u2019s Golisano Children\u2019s Hospital ( GCH ) is actively recruiting for a General or Subspecialty trained Pediatrician (i.e., Critical Care, Hospitalist Medicine) who has interest and experience in Child Abuse Pediatrics. It is anticipated that approximately 50% of the candidate\u2019s time would be spent with Child Abuse and 50% of their time spent in either General Pediatrics or their subspecialty. This Physician will join the Division of General Pediatrics, and as applicable their subspecialty division, and be part of a multidisciplinary team focused on advocacy and neglect. The Child Abuse Physician will provide medical evaluations of suspected child abuse victims at the Child Advocacy Center Buffalo ( CAC ) as well as child abuse consultations at GCH at Buffalo. Job duties include multidisciplinary team collaboration with the child abuse team at the CAC , the pediatric trauma team at GCH , and community agencies working to manage and prevent child abuse and neglect, and provide children and families with the support they need. Care is provided in conjunction with academic teaching duties for medical students and residents from the Jacobs School of Medicine and Biomedical Sciences. The successful candidate will have an academic appointment with the University commensurate to rank and experience. Compensation & Benefits Competitive salary Retirement plan contributions, no employee contribution required Health, dental, and vision insurance Malpractice coverage CME support Why Buffalo? Affordable housing and excellent schools \u201cThe City of Good Neighbors\u201d Commute-friendly Family-friendly community Four-season outdoor activities Proximity to Toronto and major Northeast cities Buffalo International Airport Medical campus with Children\u2019s hospital, Cancer center, Adult Stroke center/Adult hospital and Medical School on site. See here to learn more: University at Buffalo community. UBMD Pediatrics is one of 16 practice plans within UBMD Physicians\u2019 Group, the single largest medical group in Western New York. We provide premier health care to infants, children, adolescents and adults. In addition to primary care pediatrics, we have 15 pediatric subspecialties. Our physicians make up the academic teaching faculty within the Department of Pediatrics at the Jacobs School of Medicine and Biomedical Sciences at the University at Buffalo and Golisano Children\u2019s Hospital. University at Buffalo is an affirmative action/equal opportunity employer and, in keeping with our commitment, welcomes all to apply including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Minimum Qualifications MD, DO, or equivalent degree Board-certified/board-eligible in Pediatrics Eligible for New York State licensure Interest in academic medicine Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Driving Requirements Salary Range $0.00 Additional Salary Information The salary range reflects our good faith and reasonable estimate of the possible compensation at the time of posting, the role and associated responsibilities, and the experience, education, and training of the selected candidate. Job Type Full-Time Campus Downtown Campus Posting Alerts Special Instructions Summary Is a background check required for this posting? No Background Check Notification Contact Information Contact's Name Linda Ramsey Contact's Pronouns Contact's Title Department Administrator Contact's Email lkramsey@buffalo.edu Contact's Phone 716-323-0011 Posting Dates Posted 06/02/2026 Deadline for Applicants Open Until Filled Date to be filled References Number of References Required 3 Reference Cutoff Date Instructions 